// Bundled by cg-bundler from the `ice-and-fire-bot-plan` package. Do not edit this file:
// change the sources in the repository and bundle again.
// Workspace crates included below: cg_core, cg_pack, ice_and_fire_early, ice_and_fire_engine, ice_and_fire_opening, ice_and_fire_policy, ice_and_fire_tactics.

//! Plan bot for A Code of Ice and Fire (experiments E002 to E004, E010): a search
//! after the contest's winner (`games/ice-and-fire/research/README.md`,
//! "What strong bots do"), with a planned opening
//! (`games/ice-and-fire/research/early-game.md`).
//!
//! A turn is a list of commands, the plan. The bot first looks for a lethal
//! move or chain of trainings and plays it. Until the middle game (it can pay
//! a chain of trainings to an enemy cell), and at most to game turn 6 (E067:
//! the opening buys nothing at turn 7, the search does), it plays the opening
//! (`crate::ice_and_fire_opening::planned` with the solo planner, E010): v003's
//! opening by rules, with weights for a compact shape and a pull toward the
//! enemy HQ chosen turn by turn by a beam search over our next 9 turns as if
//! the opponent passed (`crate::ice_and_fire_opening::solo`), which rates the
//! territory, the income and the gold, less the cells one capture would cut
//! off, the joints and the ends of lines, plus the land nearer us than the
//! enemy and the progress toward its HQ; it builds no mine and weighs land
//! above income (E034), and a cell is worth less for each of our units next
//! to it, so that units spread (E051). The plan is made on the first turn,
//! kept while our side of the board is as predicted, and made again within
//! the turn's time otherwise. Else it climbs: from
//! the start of the turn it keeps adding the single action (a move, a
//! training, a tower, a mine, one of the best cuts, a lethal chain) that most
//! raises the score of the plan, until none does or the time is up. The score
//! of a plan is the worst evaluation of the state after it, our turn ended,
//! over the replies of the opponent in a memory (its lethal chain, its best
//! cuts, bronze's greedy turn and its own plan, the same climb from its seat
//! with up to 300 tries (E019), each answered by the plan). After a climb
//! the opponent's replies to the plan are added to the memory and the plan is
//! searched again against them; when that teaches nothing new, the next climb
//! may not start with the first action of a plan found so far (E014), until
//! the time is up. The plan that scores best against the whole memory and
//! its own replies (E027) is played; a plan whose replies the time cut is
//! checked against them first, before the hard limit. Cuts are chains of up to 5 trainings (E014). The evaluation
//! counts a side that cannot pay its upkeep as having lost its units, and a
//! level-2 unit as worth 5 rather than its training cost of 20 (E020).
//!
//! The input never names the league, so the bot plays with all the rules
//! (Bronze). Each command sent was accepted by the engine, in order, on a
//! scratch copy of the state. A turn whose text does not read as a state is
//! answered with `WAIT`; a bad count line or input that ends in the middle of
//! a turn ends the bot with exit code 1. The time budget of a turn is 45 ms
//! times `CG_TIME_SCALE`, 800 ms on the first turn (of CodinGame's 1,000
//! ms), of which the opening's plan takes about 610 ms. With `CG_FIXED_ITERS`
//! set to a positive number (tests only, never on CodinGame) a turn has no
//! deadline: the opening searches all its widths and the middle game stops
//! after that many tries, so that a game replays exactly (ADR 0025). Debug
//! output goes to stderr only.
//!
//! Built with `--features analysis`, the binary also measures a bank of
//! positions (`bank`) and times the search on one (`speed`), see the
//! `analysis` module; bots never carry that code.

mod actions {
    //! The actions of the search: what can be added to a plan in a state.
    //!
    //! Single commands: each move of a movable unit to a neighbouring cell it may
    //! enter, each training at the lowest level that may enter a cell (so a
    //! higher level only where it kills a unit or passes a tower), each tower on a
    //! border cell that guards something (E026, [`guards`]) and each mine on a
    //! mine spot. Macro actions: the best few cuts
    //! of the enemy's territory, the lethal chain of trainings, if there is
    //! one, and with [`STEP_GUARD`] a step into a neutral cell with a guard on
    //! the cell left behind (E070). Every action is checked by applying it on a clone, so a list may hold
    //! some that the rules refuse.

    use crate::ice_and_fire_engine::state::BUILD_COST;
    use crate::ice_and_fire_engine::{Bits, Command, State, HQ, SIZE};
    use crate::ice_and_fire_tactics::chain::{chain_to, cost_to};
    use crate::ice_and_fire_tactics::cut::cuts;

    use crate::eval::threatened;

    /// Whether a tower that raises the enemy's chain to our HQ, while the enemy
    /// can pay for it within two of its turns, is offered too (E026's second
    /// variant).
    pub const HQ_GUARD: bool = true;

    /// Whether a tower on `cell` guards something for the player to act (E026):
    /// it lowers the cells of ours the enemy can take at its next turn
    /// ([`threatened`]), or, with [`HQ_GUARD`], it raises the enemy's chain to
    /// our HQ while that chain costs at most the enemy's gold plus two of its
    /// incomes. `threats` is `threatened(state, me)`, `reach` the cells the
    /// enemy's chains reach behind it, and `chain` the enemy's chain to our HQ,
    /// before the tower.
    ///
    /// A tower only makes harder to enter its own cell and the cells next to
    /// it (RULES.md, protection), so where none of them is in `reach` it cannot
    /// lower `threats`, and the state is not copied unless the HQ guard may
    /// apply: the same answer, cheaper.
    fn guards(state: &State, cell: usize, threats: i64, reach: Bits, chain: i64) -> bool {
        let me = state.to_act();
        let enemy = 1 - me;
        let hq_guard = HQ_GUARD && chain <= state.gold(enemy) + 2 * state.income(enemy).max(0);
        let zone = Bits::cell(cell) | Bits::cell(cell).neighbours();
        if !hq_guard && (zone & reach).is_empty() {
            return false;
        }
        let (x, y) = xy(cell);
        let mut after = state.clone();
        if !after.apply(Command::BuildTower { x, y }) {
            return false;
        }
        if threatened(&after, me) < threats {
            return true;
        }
        hq_guard && cost_to(&after, enemy, false, HQ[me]) > chain
    }

    /// Whether a tower is also offered on each free border cell that would
    /// guard a frontier cell of ours not yet guarded (E068's tower wall).
    pub const WALL_TOWERS: bool = false;

    /// Which of our own empty active cells get a training offered (E045): 0,
    /// all of them (v021); 1, those next to a cell that is not active for us;
    /// 2, none (E045's screening). E044's blockers may still offer a unit on a
    /// cell a reply enters.
    pub const OWN_CELLS: u8 = 2;

    /// The step-and-guard macro action (E070): a unit steps into a neutral cell
    /// from a cell of ours the enemy can reach at its next turn, and that cell
    /// is guarded at once, so that a unit that holds the front can advance.
    /// 0: none (v028); 1: a tower on the cell it leaves; 2: a level-1 training
    /// on the cell it leaves.
    pub const STEP_GUARD: u8 = 1;

    /// The fall-back-and-guard macro action (E076, after zasmu's games): a unit
    /// on a cell of ours the enemy can reach at its next turn steps onto a cell
    /// that is owned (E070 offers the steps into neutral cells), and the cell
    /// it leaves gets a tower. 0: none (v030); 1: steps onto our cells farther
    /// from the enemy HQ (back); 2: steps onto our cells next to an enemy cell
    /// (along the border, ice-and-fire-v031); 3: steps onto any of our cells
    /// or an enemy cell other than its HQ.
    pub const FALL_BACK: u8 = 2;

    /// The rush from the tip (E076): chains of level-1 trainings into neutral
    /// cells, from the trainable neutral cells nearest the enemy HQ, each next
    /// cell the neutral neighbour nearest it, of 2 up to this many trainings;
    /// 0 for none (v030).
    pub const RUSH_LENGTH: usize = 0;

    /// The starts of [`RUSH_LENGTH`]'s chains: this many trainable neutral
    /// cells, the nearest the enemy HQ first (or, with [`RUSH_GOAL`], this many
    /// goals, the nearest first).
    pub const RUSH_STARTS: usize = 2;

    /// Whether [`RUSH_LENGTH`]'s chains head for goals rather than the enemy
    /// HQ (the owner's choice, 2026-11-20): the middle chokes we do not hold,
    /// then, once each of them is claimed, the band cells we do not hold
    /// (`eval::goal_zones`). A goal is claimed when one of our units is no
    /// farther from it than our nearest trainable cell and nearer to it than
    /// every enemy unit. Each chain starts at the trainable cell nearest its
    /// goal and steps toward it. False: the enemy HQ (rounds 1 to 3).
    pub const RUSH_GOAL: bool = false;

    /// With [`RUSH_GOAL`], whether goals the enemy wins are left out (the
    /// owner's choice, 2026-11-20): those it holds, and those one of its units
    /// is nearer to than our nearest trainable cell.
    pub const RUSH_SKIP_ENEMY: bool = false;

    /// Whether each rush chain is also offered as a leapfrog (the owner's
    /// choice, 2026-11-20, after zasmu trains at the tip once its units have
    /// moved): a movable unit of ours next to the chain's first cell steps onto
    /// it, and the trainings go on from there.
    pub const RUSH_LEAP: bool = false;

    /// Whether the centre cells the enemy can grab are defended (the owner's
    /// choices, 2026-11-20): the middle chokes and band cells it reaches before
    /// our nearest trainable cell, and those of ours its chains reach at its
    /// next turn (`eval::reach`), the nearest to our land first, at most twice
    /// [`RUSH_STARTS`]. For each: the chain of level-1 trainings that takes it
    /// this turn, when one of at most [`RUSH_LENGTH`] (3 if 0) trainings
    /// reaches it; and a tower on it, if it is ours, or on our cells next to
    /// it. Blocking the enemy's path needs no action of its own: every training
    /// on a trainable cell is offered.
    pub const RUSH_DEFEND: bool = false;

    /// Cuts offered as macro actions.
    pub const MACRO_CUTS: usize = 4;
    /// Longest cut, in trainings: 5 since E014 (4 before).
    pub const CUT_LENGTH: usize = 5;

    /// One step of a plan: a command, or a short chain of commands that go
    /// together.
    #[derive(Clone)]
    pub enum Action {
        One(Command),
        Many(Vec<Command>),
    }

    impl Action {
        /// The commands, in the order they are applied.
        pub fn commands(&self) -> &[Command] {
            match self {
                Action::One(command) => std::slice::from_ref(command),
                Action::Many(commands) => commands,
            }
        }
    }

    pub fn xy(cell: usize) -> (u8, u8) {
        ((cell % SIZE) as u8, (cell / SIZE) as u8)
    }

    /// The actions for the player to act in `state`, in `out` (cleared first), in
    /// a fixed order.
    pub fn generate(state: &State, out: &mut Vec<Action>) {
        out.clear();
        if state.outcome().is_some() {
            return;
        }
        let me = state.to_act();
        let max = state.league().max_level();
        let mut enter = [Bits::EMPTY; 4];
        for level in 1..=max {
            enter[usize::from(level)] = state.enterable(me, level);
        }

        // Moves.
        for from in state.movable_units().iter() {
            let Some((id, level)) = state.unit_at(from) else {
                continue;
            };
            let steps = Bits::cell(from).neighbours() & enter[usize::from(level)];
            for to in steps.iter() {
                let (x, y) = xy(to);
                out.push(Action::One(Command::Move { id, x, y }));
            }
        }

        // Trainings, at the lowest level that may enter the cell; on our own
        // cells as OWN_CELLS says (E045).
        let gold = state.gold(me);
        // Our inactive cells stay offered: a training there joins them again.
        let active = state.active(me);
        let near = state.near_active(me);
        let trainable = match OWN_CELLS {
            0 => near,
            1 => {
                let border = state.map().valid.and_not(active).neighbours() & active;
                near.and_not(active) | border
            }
            _ => near.and_not(active),
        };
        for level in 1..=max {
            let cost = 10 * i64::from(level);
            if gold < cost {
                break;
            }
            let mut cells = trainable & enter[usize::from(level)];
            for lower in 1..level {
                cells = cells.and_not(enter[usize::from(lower)]);
            }
            for cell in cells.iter() {
                let (x, y) = xy(cell);
                out.push(Action::One(Command::Train { level, x, y }));
            }
        }

        // Buildings.
        if gold >= BUILD_COST {
            let free = state.owned(me) & near & state.empty_cells();
            if state.league().allows_mines() {
                for cell in (free & state.map().spots).iter() {
                    let (x, y) = xy(cell);
                    out.push(Action::One(Command::BuildMine { x, y }));
                }
            }
            if state.league().allows_towers() {
                // Towers only on cells next to a cell that is not ours.
                let border = state.map().valid.and_not(state.owned(me)).neighbours();
                let cells = (free & border).and_not(state.map().spots);
                // `threatened(state, me)`, keeping the enemy's reach.
                let reach = crate::eval::reach(state, 1 - me);
                let threats = i64::from((reach & state.active(me)).count());
                let chain = cost_to(state, 1 - me, false, HQ[me]);
                // Frontier cells of ours not yet guarded by a tower (E068).
                let open = if WALL_TOWERS {
                    let (front, guarded) = crate::eval::frontier(state, me);
                    front.and_not(guarded)
                } else {
                    Bits::EMPTY
                };
                for cell in cells.iter().filter(|&cell| {
                    let zone = Bits::cell(cell) | Bits::cell(cell).neighbours();
                    !(zone & open).is_empty() || guards(state, cell, threats, reach, chain)
                }) {
                    let (x, y) = xy(cell);
                    out.push(Action::One(Command::BuildTower { x, y }));
                }
            }
        }

        // Step and guard (E070): the step, then the cell left behind guarded.
        let guard_cost = match STEP_GUARD {
            1 => BUILD_COST,
            2 => 10,
            _ => i64::MAX,
        };
        if gold >= guard_cost {
            let reach = crate::eval::reach(state, 1 - me);
            let neutral = state
                .map()
                .valid
                .and_not(state.owned(me) | state.owned(1 - me));
            for from in (state.movable_units() & reach).iter() {
                let Some((id, level)) = state.unit_at(from) else {
                    continue;
                };
                let steps = Bits::cell(from).neighbours() & enter[usize::from(level)] & neutral;
                let (fx, fy) = xy(from);
                let guard = if STEP_GUARD == 1 {
                    if state.map().spots.test(from) {
                        continue;
                    }
                    Command::BuildTower { x: fx, y: fy }
                } else {
                    Command::Train {
                        level: 1,
                        x: fx,
                        y: fy,
                    }
                };
                for to in steps.iter() {
                    let (x, y) = xy(to);
                    out.push(Action::Many(vec![Command::Move { id, x, y }, guard]));
                }
            }
        }

        // Fall back and guard (E076): a step onto an owned cell, then a tower
        // on the cell left behind.
        if FALL_BACK != 0 && gold >= BUILD_COST && state.league().allows_towers() {
            fall_back(state, &enter, out);
        }

        // Rush from the tip (E076): chains of level-1 trainings toward the
        // enemy HQ.
        if RUSH_LENGTH != 0 && gold >= 20 {
            rush(state, enter[1], gold, out);
        }

        // Defend the centre cells the enemy can grab (E076).
        if RUSH_DEFEND {
            defend(state, enter[1], gold, out);
        }

        // Macro actions: the best cuts, and the lethal chain. A cut of one
        // training is a single training already.
        for cut in cuts(state, CUT_LENGTH, gold, MACRO_CUTS) {
            if cut.commands.len() > 1 {
                out.push(Action::Many(cut.commands));
            }
        }
        if let Some(chain) = chain_to(state, HQ[1 - me], gold) {
            if chain.commands.len() > 1 {
                out.push(Action::Many(chain.commands));
            }
        }
    }

    /// The fall-back-and-guard actions (E076, [`FALL_BACK`]) of the player to
    /// act, with `enter` as [`generate`] has it.
    fn fall_back(state: &State, enter: &[Bits; 4], out: &mut Vec<Action>) {
        let me = state.to_act();
        let enemy = 1 - me;
        let reach = crate::eval::reach(state, enemy);
        let ours = state.owned(me);
        let theirs = state.owned(enemy);
        let border = theirs.neighbours();
        let spots = state.map().spots;
        for from in (state.movable_units() & reach & state.active(me)).iter() {
            if spots.test(from) {
                continue;
            }
            let Some((id, level)) = state.unit_at(from) else {
                continue;
            };
            let away = state.map().distance(from, HQ[enemy]);
            let steps = Bits::cell(from).neighbours() & enter[usize::from(level)];
            let (fx, fy) = xy(from);
            for to in steps.iter() {
                let allowed = match FALL_BACK {
                    1 => ours.test(to) && state.map().distance(to, HQ[enemy]) > away,
                    2 => ours.test(to) && border.test(to),
                    // A step onto the enemy HQ wins: it is offered alone.
                    _ => ours.test(to) || (theirs.test(to) && to != HQ[enemy]),
                };
                if !allowed {
                    continue;
                }
                let (x, y) = xy(to);
                out.push(Action::Many(vec![
                    Command::Move { id, x, y },
                    Command::BuildTower { x: fx, y: fy },
                ]));
            }
        }
    }

    /// The rush-from-the-tip actions (E076, [`RUSH_LENGTH`]): `level1` is where
    /// a level-1 unit of the player to act may go.
    fn rush(state: &State, level1: Bits, gold: i64, out: &mut Vec<Action>) {
        let me = state.to_act();
        let map = state.map();
        let neutral = map.valid.and_not(state.owned(me) | state.owned(1 - me));
        let open = neutral & level1;
        let trainable: Vec<usize> = (state.active(me).neighbours() & open).iter().collect();
        if trainable.is_empty() {
            return;
        }
        // The chains' starts, each with the cell it heads for.
        let nearest = |target: usize| {
            trainable
                .iter()
                .copied()
                .min_by_key(|&cell| (map.distance(cell, target), cell))
        };
        let mut chains: Vec<(usize, usize)> = Vec::new();
        if RUSH_GOAL {
            for goal in rush_goals(state, &trainable) {
                if let Some(start) = nearest(goal) {
                    chains.push((start, goal));
                }
            }
        } else {
            let target = HQ[1 - me];
            let mut starts = trainable.clone();
            starts.sort_by_key(|&cell| (map.distance(cell, target), cell));
            starts.truncate(RUSH_STARTS);
            chains.extend(starts.into_iter().map(|start| (start, target)));
        }
        let most = usize::try_from(gold / 10).unwrap_or(0).min(RUSH_LENGTH);
        for (start, target) in chains {
            let mut chain = vec![start];
            let mut taken = Bits::cell(start);
            while chain.len() < most {
                let last = chain[chain.len() - 1];
                if last == target {
                    break;
                }
                let next = (Bits::cell(last).neighbours() & open)
                    .and_not(taken)
                    .iter()
                    .min_by_key(|&cell| (map.distance(cell, target), cell));
                let Some(next) = next else {
                    break;
                };
                chain.push(next);
                taken.set(next);
                let commands = chain
                    .iter()
                    .map(|&cell| {
                        let (x, y) = xy(cell);
                        Command::Train { level: 1, x, y }
                    })
                    .collect();
                out.push(Action::Many(commands));
            }
            if RUSH_LEAP {
                leapfrogs(state, &chain, out);
            }
        }
    }

    /// The leapfrogs of `chain` ([`RUSH_LEAP`]): for each movable unit of ours
    /// next to the chain's first cell that may enter it, the step onto it, then
    /// the trainings of the chain's next cells, one more each time.
    fn leapfrogs(state: &State, chain: &[usize], out: &mut Vec<Action>) {
        let me = state.to_act();
        let start = chain[0];
        let movers = state.movable_units() & state.units(me) & Bits::cell(start).neighbours();
        for from in movers.iter() {
            let Some((id, level)) = state.unit_at(from) else {
                continue;
            };
            if !state.enterable(me, level).test(start) {
                continue;
            }
            let (x, y) = xy(start);
            let mut commands = vec![Command::Move { id, x, y }];
            for &cell in &chain[1..] {
                let (x, y) = xy(cell);
                commands.push(Command::Train { level: 1, x, y });
                out.push(Action::Many(commands.clone()));
            }
        }
    }

    /// The goals of [`RUSH_GOAL`]'s chains, the nearest to `trainable` (our
    /// trainable cells) first, at most [`RUSH_STARTS`]: the middle chokes we do
    /// not hold and no unit of ours claims, or, when there is none, the band
    /// cells alike.
    pub fn rush_goals(state: &State, trainable: &[usize]) -> Vec<usize> {
        let me = state.to_act();
        let map = state.map();
        let (band, chokes) = crate::eval::goal_zones(state);
        let ours: Vec<usize> = state.units(me).iter().collect();
        let theirs: Vec<usize> = state.units(1 - me).iter().collect();
        let from_trainable = |goal: usize| {
            trainable
                .iter()
                .map(|&cell| map.distance(cell, goal))
                .min()
                .unwrap_or(u8::MAX)
        };
        let claimed = |goal: usize| {
            let reach = from_trainable(goal);
            ours.iter().any(|&unit| {
                let d = map.distance(unit, goal);
                d <= reach && theirs.iter().all(|&enemy| d < map.distance(enemy, goal))
            })
        };
        // RUSH_SKIP_ENEMY: the enemy holds it, or one of its units is nearer.
        let lost = |goal: usize| {
            RUSH_SKIP_ENEMY
                && (state.owned(1 - me).test(goal)
                    || theirs
                        .iter()
                        .any(|&enemy| map.distance(enemy, goal) < from_trainable(goal)))
        };
        let open = |cells: Bits| -> Vec<usize> {
            let mut goals: Vec<usize> = cells
                .and_not(state.owned(me))
                .iter()
                .filter(|&goal| from_trainable(goal) != u8::MAX && !claimed(goal) && !lost(goal))
                .collect();
            goals.sort_by_key(|&goal| (from_trainable(goal), goal));
            goals
        };
        let mut goals = open(chokes);
        if goals.is_empty() {
            goals = open(band);
        }
        goals.truncate(RUSH_STARTS);
        goals
    }

    /// The centre cells [`RUSH_DEFEND`] defends: chokes and band cells the
    /// enemy reaches first (not ours) or can take at its next turn (ours), the
    /// nearest to our active land first.
    pub fn contested(state: &State) -> Vec<usize> {
        let me = state.to_act();
        let map = state.map();
        let (band, chokes) = crate::eval::goal_zones(state);
        let active = state.active(me);
        let ours = state.owned(me);
        let reach = crate::eval::reach(state, 1 - me);
        let theirs: Vec<usize> = state.units(1 - me).iter().collect();
        let from_land = |cell: usize| {
            active
                .iter()
                .map(|a| map.distance(a, cell))
                .min()
                .unwrap_or(u8::MAX)
        };
        let mut cells: Vec<usize> = (band | chokes)
            .iter()
            .filter(|&cell| {
                if ours.test(cell) {
                    active.test(cell) && reach.test(cell)
                } else {
                    !state.owned(1 - me).test(cell)
                        && theirs
                            .iter()
                            .any(|&e| map.distance(e, cell) < from_land(cell))
                }
            })
            .collect();
        cells.sort_by_key(|&cell| (u8::from(!chokes.test(cell)), from_land(cell), cell));
        cells.truncate(2 * RUSH_STARTS);
        cells
    }

    /// The [`RUSH_DEFEND`] actions: `level1` is where a level-1 unit of the
    /// player to act may go.
    fn defend(state: &State, level1: Bits, gold: i64, out: &mut Vec<Action>) {
        let me = state.to_act();
        let map = state.map();
        let neutral = map.valid.and_not(state.owned(me) | state.owned(1 - me));
        let open = neutral & level1;
        let active = state.active(me);
        let free = active & state.empty_cells();
        let longest = if RUSH_LENGTH == 0 { 3 } else { RUSH_LENGTH };
        for cell in contested(state) {
            if !state.owned(me).test(cell) {
                // Train onto it first: the shortest chain from our land.
                let start = (active.neighbours() & open)
                    .iter()
                    .min_by_key(|&c| (map.distance(c, cell), c));
                if let Some(start) = start {
                    let mut chain = vec![start];
                    let mut taken = Bits::cell(start);
                    while chain[chain.len() - 1] != cell && chain.len() < longest {
                        let last = chain[chain.len() - 1];
                        let next = (Bits::cell(last).neighbours() & open)
                            .and_not(taken)
                            .iter()
                            .min_by_key(|&c| (map.distance(c, cell), c));
                        let Some(next) = next else {
                            break;
                        };
                        chain.push(next);
                        taken.set(next);
                    }
                    let cost = 10 * i64::try_from(chain.len()).unwrap_or(i64::MAX);
                    if chain.len() >= 2 && chain[chain.len() - 1] == cell && cost <= gold {
                        let commands = chain
                            .iter()
                            .map(|&c| {
                                let (x, y) = xy(c);
                                Command::Train { level: 1, x, y }
                            })
                            .collect();
                        out.push(Action::Many(commands));
                    }
                }
            }
            // A tower on it or behind it.
            if gold >= BUILD_COST && state.league().allows_towers() {
                let spots = (Bits::cell(cell) | Bits::cell(cell).neighbours()) & free;
                for tower in spots.and_not(map.spots).iter() {
                    let (x, y) = xy(tower);
                    out.push(Action::One(Command::BuildTower { x, y }));
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
mod eval {
    //! The bot's evaluation of a state, from the point of view of `seat`.
    //!
    //! It starts as the shared static evaluation
    //! (`crate::ice_and_fire_tactics::eval::evaluate`: what each side has, the threat to
    //! the HQ and how far each side is from affording the chain to the other's
    //! HQ). Terms of the bot's own go here, each documented:
    //!
    //! - **Debt** (E003): a side whose gold plus income is below 0 loses all its
    //!   units at its next start of turn (RULES.md), so twice the training cost
    //!   of its units on active cells is taken from its score: once for the
    //!   units the shared evaluation counts, once for the loss.
    //! - **Shape** (E010): a side's territory is weak where one capture cuts
    //!   cells off from its HQ. For each side, [`SHAPE`] times the number of its
    //!   joints (active cells whose loss cuts others off) and the most cells
    //!   one loss cuts off (`crate::ice_and_fire_opening::solo::severed`) is taken from
    //!   its score, as the opening's plans do.
    //! - **Level-2 units** (E020): a level-2 unit costs 4 gold of upkeep a turn
    //!   against 1 for a level-1 one, and in v008's games a side with more of
    //!   them than the score said won less often: each counts [`LEVEL2_DISCOUNT`]
    //!   less than its training cost, 5 in all.
    //! - **Threatened cells** (E023): in v009's games a cut the enemy could
    //!   first afford with one more income was made within one turn about a
    //!   quarter of the time, so a cell it can take at its next turn counts 0.75
    //!   of a cell's value (4 as a cell, 3 as its income): [`threatened`] cells
    //!   cost a side `7 / 4` each (`5 / 4` since E037).
    //! - **Mines** (E033): the shared evaluation counts a mine as its income of
    //!   4, three times, 12 against the 15 gold it costs, so a climb rarely
    //!   gained by building one, while the top 10 of CodinGame build one in a
    //!   fifth of their games at every turn from turn 9, once their territory
    //!   is large. A mine on an active cell that the enemy cannot take at its
    //!   next turn counts one more for every [`MINE_PER_CELLS`] active cells of
    //!   its side ([`mine_bonus`]): little on a small territory, 9 at 36 cells.
    //! - **Units' moves** (E037): the threatened cells of E023 were those the
    //!   enemy's chains of trainings reach, so a unit at the front threatened
    //!   nothing, though a move costs no gold. The enemy's units on its active
    //!   cells of at least level [`MOVER_LEVEL`] now step first onto every
    //!   neighbour they may enter, as `crate::ice_and_fire_tactics::chain::Reach` lets
    //!   units do, and the chains go on from there; a threatened cell costs
    //!   [`THREAT_QUARTERS`] quarters.
    //! - **Standing threat** (E042): in v014's CodinGame games the top 10 could
    //!   pay, after 28% of their long chains, for a chain of trainings to our
    //!   HQ at their next turn (we after 4% of ours), so that punishing their
    //!   chain would leave our HQ open; the pressure term stops counting once a
    //!   side can pay. A side that can pays counts [`standing`] more.
    //! - **Moves toward the HQ** (E043): the chain to the enemy HQ behind the
    //!   pressure term and [`standing`] left moves out; with
    //!   [`MARGIN_MOVER_LEVEL`], a side's units of that level or more on its
    //!   active cells step first, at no cost, as in E037's reach.
    //! - **Upkeep of strong units** (E036): the shared evaluation counts income
    //!   three times, and income is net of upkeep, so a level-3 unit (upkeep 20)
    //!   costs 60 there and a level-2 unit (upkeep 4) 12, beyond their training
    //!   cost: a level-3 training scores about -50 before what it takes. Each
    //!   level-2 and level-3 unit on an active cell gives back the upkeep of
    //!   the turns beyond [`UPKEEP_TURNS`].
    //! - **Tower wall** (E068): in its CodinGame games against us, zasmu guards
    //!   75 to 85% of its frontier cells with towers (the other top players and
    //!   we about 50%) and keeps its upkeep low. Each active cell of a side next
    //!   to an enemy cell that is one of its active towers or next to one counts
    //!   [`WALL`] more ([`wall`]).
    //! - **The opening's goal** (E073): the opening chooses its plans by the
    //!   share of the contested band they claim (cells within [`GOAL_BAND`]
    //!   rings of the frontline, `crate::ice_and_fire_opening::solo::rings`), and the
    //!   search takes over at game turn 7 without it. Until game turn
    //!   [`GOAL_UNTIL`], band cells near a side's land, held by it, guarded by
    //!   its towers, and the middle chokes it holds count for it ([`goal`]).
    //! - **Both flanks** (E095): in v032's CodinGame games we hold as much land
    //!   as the top players to game turn 10, but on one flank: both flanks by
    //!   game turn 8 in 12 to 14% of our games against 33 to 41% of theirs.
    //!   Until game turn [`FLANK_UNTIL`], a side's active cells on its weaker
    //!   flank, up to [`FLANK_CAP`], count [`FLANK`] each for it ([`flank`]):
    //!   off, since it lost the screening at every weight tried (4, 8, 16);
    //!   E095's opening order holds both flanks instead.

    use crate::ice_and_fire_engine::{Bits, State, CELLS, HQ, SIZE};
    use crate::ice_and_fire_tactics::chain::reach_within_moving;
    use crate::ice_and_fire_tactics::eval::{evaluate_with_movers, pressure, side_parts};

    /// The lowest level of a unit whose moves count in [`exposed`] (E037): 1 to
    /// 3, or 4 for none (v016). Level 2 won the screening.
    pub const MOVER_LEVEL: u8 = 2;

    /// What a threatened cell costs its side, in quarters: 7 in E023 (a quarter
    /// of a cell's value of 7), 5 since E037, which finds more of them.
    pub const THREAT_QUARTERS: i64 = 5;

    /// The units of `seat` whose moves count in [`exposed`]: those on its active
    /// cells of at least [`MOVER_LEVEL`], all of which may move at its next turn.
    fn movers(state: &State, seat: usize) -> Bits {
        movers_from(state, seat, MOVER_LEVEL)
    }

    /// The units of `seat` on its active cells of at least level `from` (none
    /// when `from` is above 3).
    pub(crate) fn movers_from(state: &State, seat: usize, from: u8) -> Bits {
        let mut movers = Bits::EMPTY;
        if from > 3 {
            return movers;
        }
        for cell in (state.units(seat) & state.active(seat)).iter() {
            if state.unit_level(cell).is_some_and(|level| level >= from) {
                movers |= Bits::cell(cell);
            }
        }
        movers
    }

    /// The cells, other than its active cells, that `side` can take at its next
    /// turn: those its chains of trainings reach for its gold plus its income,
    /// after its [`movers`] step (E037; the pressure term leaves moves out).
    pub fn reach(state: &State, side: usize) -> Bits {
        let budget = state.gold(side) + state.income(side);
        reach_within_moving(state, side, movers(state, side), budget)
    }

    /// The active cells of `seat` that the enemy can take at its next turn
    /// ([`reach`]).
    pub(crate) fn exposed(state: &State, seat: usize) -> Bits {
        reach(state, 1 - seat) & state.active(seat)
    }

    /// The number of active cells of `seat` that the enemy can take at its next
    /// turn ([`exposed`]).
    pub fn threatened(state: &State, seat: usize) -> i64 {
        i64::from(exposed(state, seat).count())
    }

    /// The active cells of a side for which each of its mines counts one more
    /// than its income (E033).
    pub const MINE_PER_CELLS: i64 = 4;

    /// What each mine of a side with `cells` active cells counts beyond its
    /// income.
    pub fn mine_bonus(cells: i64) -> i64 {
        cells / MINE_PER_CELLS
    }

    /// What the mines of `seat` count beyond their income: [`mine_bonus`] for
    /// each on its active cells that the enemy cannot take at its next turn.
    /// `exposed` is `exposed(state, seat)`.
    pub(crate) fn mines(state: &State, seat: usize, exposed: Bits) -> i64 {
        let active = state.active(seat);
        let mines = (state.mines() & active).and_not(exposed);
        let cells = i64::from(active.count());
        let bonus = if state.game_turn() <= EARLY_MINE_TURN {
            cells / EARLY_MINE_PER_CELLS + EARLY_MINE_BONUS
        } else {
            mine_bonus(cells)
        };
        bonus * i64::from(mines.count())
    }

    /// The last game turn on which a safe mine counts [`EARLY_MINE_BONUS`] more
    /// and one more per [`EARLY_MINE_PER_CELLS`] active cells (E058): 0 for
    /// none (v024); 15 won the screening (12 and 18 did less).
    pub const EARLY_MINE_TURN: u32 = 15;

    /// What a safe mine counts more until [`EARLY_MINE_TURN`] (E058): 6 won the
    /// screening (4 and 8 did less).
    pub const EARLY_MINE_BONUS: i64 = 6;

    /// The active cells for which a safe mine counts one more until
    /// [`EARLY_MINE_TURN`] (E058): [`MINE_PER_CELLS`] in v024.
    pub const EARLY_MINE_PER_CELLS: i64 = MINE_PER_CELLS;

    /// The weight of a joint and of a cell that one capture cuts off.
    const SHAPE: i64 = 2;

    /// Which joints the shape term counts (E081, after the diagnosis of E080:
    /// a joint deep in our land, beside the HQ, made the search train units
    /// behind its own lines): 0, all of them (v031); 1, only those at most
    /// [`SHAPE_NEAR`] steps from the enemy's active land; 2, each weighted by
    /// its distance from it, fully up to [`SHAPE_NEAR`] steps, then less and
    /// less to nothing at [`SHAPE_FAR`]. 1 with 3 steps (k3) is
    /// ice-and-fire-v032: +75.4 and +67.7 in screening on two seeds.
    pub const SHAPE_REACH: u8 = 1;
    /// See [`SHAPE_REACH`].
    pub const SHAPE_NEAR: u8 = 3;
    /// See [`SHAPE_REACH`].
    pub const SHAPE_FAR: u8 = 6;

    /// The weight in quarters of a joint `d` steps from the enemy's active land
    /// by [`SHAPE_REACH`]'s rule `mode`.
    pub fn joint_weight(mode: u8, near: u8, far: u8, d: u8) -> u8 {
        match mode {
            0 => 4,
            1 if d <= near => 4,
            1 => 0,
            _ if d <= near => 4,
            _ if d >= far => 0,
            _ => (4 * u32::from(far - d) / u32::from(far - near)) as u8,
        }
    }

    /// The weakness of `seat`'s shape: its joints plus the most cells that one
    /// capture cuts off, as `crate::ice_and_fire_opening::solo::severed` counts them,
    /// each joint weighted by [`SHAPE_REACH`]. The same depth-first search,
    /// with arrays of bytes and only these two numbers kept, since it runs
    /// twice in every evaluation: the cells one capture cuts off do not depend
    /// on the order of the search.
    fn weakness(state: &State, seat: usize) -> i64 {
        let active = state.active(seat);
        // With SHAPE_REACH, the weakness also depends on the enemy's land.
        let enemy = if SHAPE_REACH == 0 {
            Bits::EMPTY
        } else {
            state.active(1 - seat)
        };
        let [a, b, c] = active.words();
        let [e, f, g] = enemy.words();
        let mut hash = (a
            ^ b.rotate_left(21)
            ^ c.rotate_left(42)
            ^ (e ^ f.rotate_left(13) ^ g.rotate_left(37)).wrapping_mul(0x2545_f491_4f6c_dd1d)
            ^ seat as u64)
            .wrapping_mul(0x9e37_79b9_7f4a_7c15);
        hash ^= hash >> 29;
        let index = (hash as usize) & (WEAKNESS_SLOTS - 1);
        WEAKNESS.with(|cache| {
            let mut cache = cache.borrow_mut();
            let slot = &mut cache[index];
            if slot.0 == active && slot.1 == enemy && slot.2 == seat as u8 + 1 {
                return slot.3;
            }
            let value = if SHAPE_REACH == 0 {
                weakness_of(active, HQ[seat])
            } else if SHAPE_REACH == 1 {
                // The cells within SHAPE_NEAR steps of the enemy's land, as
                // `econ::distances` counts steps (through cells of the map).
                let valid = state.map().valid;
                let mut near = enemy & valid;
                for _ in 0..SHAPE_NEAR {
                    near = (near | near.neighbours()) & valid;
                }
                weakness_near(active, HQ[seat], near)
            } else {
                let d = crate::ice_and_fire_opening::econ::distances(state, enemy);
                let mut weights = [0u8; CELLS];
                for (w, &steps) in weights.iter_mut().zip(d.iter()) {
                    *w = joint_weight(SHAPE_REACH, SHAPE_NEAR, SHAPE_FAR, steps);
                }
                weakness_weighted(active, HQ[seat], &weights)
            };
            *slot = (active, enemy, seat as u8 + 1, value);
            value
        })
    }

    /// Slots of the cache of [`weakness`], a power of two.
    const WEAKNESS_SLOTS: usize = 1 << 12;

    thread_local! {
        /// [`weakness`] by territory, the enemy's active land (empty when
        /// [`SHAPE_REACH`] is 0) and seat (the seat plus one, 0 for an empty
        /// slot), so that a territory a search meets again is not searched again:
        /// most actions leave one side's territory as it was. The map is not in
        /// the key: a bot plays one map, but the analysis modes, which read
        /// positions of many games in one thread, could reuse a value of another
        /// map with the same two lands.
        static WEAKNESS: std::cell::RefCell<Vec<(Bits, Bits, u8, i64)>> =
            std::cell::RefCell::new(vec![(Bits::EMPTY, Bits::EMPTY, 0, 0); WEAKNESS_SLOTS]);
    }

    /// The cells of `active` whose removal might cut off others, for all cells
    /// at once, with bitwise operations only. Around a cell, its held
    /// neighbours (north, east, south, west) and the 4 corners between them
    /// form a ring; two neighbours a quarter-turn apart are joined on the ring
    /// when the corner between them is held. If the held neighbours make one
    /// piece on the ring (or none), taking the cell away cuts nothing off: a
    /// path through it can go round it (digital topology's test of a cell that
    /// can be removed without changing the connectivity). The held neighbours
    /// make one piece or none exactly when their number less the number of
    /// joined pairs is at most 1 (a ring held all round: 4 less 4). Both
    /// numbers are added on bit planes, three bits each, and subtracted the
    /// same way; the cells left are those where the difference is 2 or more.
    fn possibly_cut(active: Bits) -> Bits {
        // The planes: `n` holds the cells whose northern neighbour is held.
        let n = active.shift_down();
        let s = active.shift_up();
        let e = active.shift_left();
        let w = active.shift_right();
        let ne = e.shift_down();
        let nw = w.shift_down();
        let se = e.shift_up();
        let sw = w.shift_up();
        let joined = [n & ne & e, e & se & s, s & sw & w, w & nw & n];
        let xor = |a: Bits, b: Bits| (a | b).and_not(a & b);
        // Three-bit sums of four one-bit planes.
        let add4 = |[a, b, c, d]: [Bits; 4]| {
            let (s1, c1) = (xor(a, b), a & b);
            let (s2, c2) = (xor(c, d), c & d);
            let t = s1 & s2;
            let c12 = xor(c1, c2);
            (xor(s1, s2), xor(c12, t), (c1 & c2) | (t & c12))
        };
        let (h0, h1, h2) = add4([n, e, s, w]);
        let (e0, e1, e2) = add4(joined);
        // h - e, which is never negative: at least 2 when bit 1 or bit 2 is set.
        let b0 = e0.and_not(h0);
        let x1 = xor(h1, e1);
        let d1 = xor(x1, b0);
        let b1 = e1.and_not(h1) | b0.and_not(x1);
        let d2 = xor(xor(h2, e2), b1);
        active & (d1 | d2)
    }

    /// [`weakness_weighted`] when every joint near the enemy weighs 4 quarters
    /// and the others nothing ([`SHAPE_REACH`] 1), with bitwise operations:
    /// the joints are looked for only among the cells of `near` that
    /// [`possibly_cut`] leaves (about 4 of the 17 cells of our land near the
    /// enemy's in v033's CodinGame games); each one left is taken away and the
    /// land flooded again from the HQ, the cells it no longer reaches being
    /// those the joint cuts off. The same value as the depth-first search.
    pub fn weakness_near(active: Bits, root: usize, near: Bits) -> i64 {
        if !active.test(root) {
            return 0;
        }
        let total = active.count();
        let mut joints = 0i64;
        let mut most = 0i64;
        for v in (possibly_cut(active) & near).iter() {
            if v == root {
                continue;
            }
            let rest = active.and_not(Bits::cell(v));
            let mut region = Bits::cell(root);
            loop {
                let next = (region | region.neighbours()) & rest;
                if next == region {
                    break;
                }
                region = next;
            }
            let cut = i64::from(total - 1 - region.count());
            if cut > 0 {
                joints += 4;
                most = most.max(4 * cut);
            }
        }
        (joints + most) / 4
    }

    /// [`weakness`] of the territory `active` whose HQ is `root`, every joint
    /// counted.
    pub fn weakness_of(active: Bits, root: usize) -> i64 {
        weakness_weighted(active, root, &[4; CELLS])
    }

    /// [`weakness_of`] with each joint `v` weighted by `weights[v]` quarters:
    /// its count and the cells it cuts off, rounded down once at the end.
    pub fn weakness_weighted(active: Bits, root: usize, weights: &[u8; CELLS]) -> i64 {
        struct Dfs<'a> {
            weights: &'a [u8; CELLS],
            active: Bits,
            disc: [u8; CELLS],
            low: [u8; CELLS],
            size: [u8; CELLS],
            time: u8,
            joints: i64,
            most: i64,
        }
        fn visit(d: &mut Dfs<'_>, v: usize) -> u8 {
            d.time += 1;
            let disc = d.time;
            d.disc[v] = disc;
            let mut low = disc;
            let mut size = 1u8;
            let mut cut = 0u8;
            for w in (Bits::cell(v).neighbours() & d.active).iter() {
                if d.disc[w] == 0 {
                    let sub = visit(d, w);
                    size += sub;
                    low = low.min(d.low[w]);
                    if d.low[w] >= disc {
                        cut += sub;
                    }
                } else {
                    low = low.min(d.disc[w]);
                }
            }
            d.low[v] = low;
            d.size[v] = size;
            if cut > 0 && d.disc[v] > 1 {
                let w = i64::from(d.weights[v]);
                d.joints += w;
                d.most = d.most.max(w * i64::from(cut));
            }
            size
        }
        if !active.test(root) {
            return 0;
        }
        let mut d = Dfs {
            weights,
            active,
            disc: [0; CELLS],
            low: [0; CELLS],
            size: [0; CELLS],
            time: 0,
            joints: 0,
            most: 0,
        };
        visit(&mut d, root);
        (d.joints + d.most) / 4
    }

    /// The shape term of `seat`'s score: [`SHAPE`] times the other side's
    /// weakness less its own.
    pub fn shape(state: &State, seat: usize) -> i64 {
        SHAPE * (weakness(state, 1 - seat) - weakness(state, seat))
    }

    /// The training cost of the units of `seat` on active cells, if it cannot
    /// pay its upkeep, else 0.
    pub(crate) fn debt(state: &State, seat: usize) -> i64 {
        if state.gold(seat) + state.income(seat) >= 0 {
            return 0;
        }
        (state.units(seat) & state.active(seat))
            .iter()
            .filter_map(|cell| state.unit_level(cell))
            .map(|level| 10 * i64::from(level))
            .sum()
    }

    /// How much less than its training cost a level-2 unit is worth (E020).
    pub const LEVEL2_DISCOUNT: i64 = 15;

    /// The turns of upkeep the evaluation charges for a level-2 and a level-3
    /// unit (E036); the shared evaluation charges 3, its weight of income.
    pub const UPKEEP_TURNS: [i64; 2] = [3, 1];

    /// The upkeep of a level-2 and a level-3 unit (RULES.md, "Income").
    const UPKEEP: [i64; 2] = [4, 20];

    /// The level-2 and level-3 units of `seat` on active cells.
    fn strong(state: &State, seat: usize) -> [i64; 2] {
        let mut count = [0; 2];
        for cell in (state.units(seat) & state.active(seat)).iter() {
            match state.unit_level(cell) {
                Some(2) => count[0] += 1,
                Some(3) => count[1] += 1,
                _ => {}
            }
        }
        count
    }

    /// What the level-2 and level-3 units of `seat` count beyond the shared
    /// evaluation: less [`LEVEL2_DISCOUNT`] each level 2 (E020), plus the
    /// upkeep of the turns beyond [`UPKEEP_TURNS`] (E036).
    pub fn strong_units(state: &State, seat: usize) -> i64 {
        let [twos, threes] = strong(state, seat);
        let back = |level: usize| (3 - UPKEEP_TURNS[level]) * UPKEEP[level];
        -LEVEL2_DISCOUNT * twos + back(0) * twos + back(1) * threes
    }

    /// What a side that can pay, at its next turn, for its chain of trainings to
    /// the enemy HQ counts more (E042): the enemy must keep defending. 0 for
    /// nothing (v018).
    pub const HQ_BONUS: i64 = 0;
    /// Halves of the gold left after paying for that chain that count too (2,
    /// all of it, won the screening), up
    /// to [`HQ_MARGIN_CAP`] (E042).
    pub const HQ_MARGIN_HALVES: i64 = 2;
    /// The most of that gold counted.
    pub const HQ_MARGIN_CAP: i64 = 100;

    /// What a side whose margin (`crate::ice_and_fire_tactics::eval::margin`) is
    /// `margin` counts for its standing threat on the enemy HQ (E042).
    pub fn standing(margin: i64) -> i64 {
        if margin < 0 {
            return 0;
        }
        HQ_BONUS + HQ_MARGIN_HALVES * margin.min(HQ_MARGIN_CAP) / 2
    }

    /// The lowest level of a unit whose moves count in the chain to the enemy
    /// HQ of the pressure term and of [`standing`] (E043): 1 to 3, or 4 for
    /// none (v019). Level 2 won the screening.
    pub const MARGIN_MOVER_LEVEL: u8 = 2;

    /// What each step of a unit's distance to the nearest cell that is not its
    /// side's costs that side, beyond the first (E060): 0 for nothing (v025).
    /// A walk through our own land toward free or enemy cells then raises the
    /// score at each step, as the top bots' units walk for several turns; 2 won
    /// the screening (1, 3 and 4 did a little less).
    pub const IDLE_STEP: i64 = 2;

    /// The farthest distance counted (E060).
    pub const IDLE_CAP: i64 = 4;

    /// The highest level of a unit counted (E060).
    pub const IDLE_LEVEL: u8 = 3;

    /// What the units of `seat` on its active cells cost it for standing away
    /// from the cells that are not its own (E060).
    pub(crate) fn idle(state: &State, seat: usize) -> i64 {
        if IDLE_STEP == 0 {
            return 0;
        }
        let valid = state.map().valid;
        let mut units = Bits::EMPTY;
        for cell in (state.units(seat) & state.active(seat)).iter() {
            if state
                .unit_level(cell)
                .is_some_and(|level| level <= IDLE_LEVEL)
            {
                units |= Bits::cell(cell);
            }
        }
        let mut within = valid.and_not(state.owned(seat));
        let mut counted = Bits::EMPTY;
        let mut steps = 0;
        for distance in 1..=IDLE_CAP {
            within = (within | within.neighbours()) & valid;
            let here = (units & within).and_not(counted);
            steps += (distance - 1) * i64::from(here.count());
            counted |= here;
        }
        steps += IDLE_CAP * i64::from(units.and_not(counted).count());
        IDLE_STEP * steps
    }

    /// What each frontier cell of a side guarded by one of its towers counts
    /// (E068): 0 for nothing (v027).
    pub const WALL: i64 = 8;

    /// The active cells of `seat` next to an enemy cell (its frontier), and
    /// those of them that are an active tower of `seat`'s or next to one.
    pub fn frontier(state: &State, seat: usize) -> (Bits, Bits) {
        let active = state.active(seat);
        let front = active & state.owned(1 - seat).neighbours();
        let towers = state.towers() & active;
        (front, front & (towers | towers.neighbours()))
    }

    /// What the tower wall of `seat` counts (E068): [`WALL`] for each of its
    /// frontier cells guarded by one of its towers.
    pub(crate) fn wall(state: &State, seat: usize) -> i64 {
        if WALL == 0 {
            return 0;
        }
        WALL * i64::from(frontier(state, seat).1.count())
    }

    /// The opening's goal kept in the search (E073), as weights of its parts,
    /// each counted for `seat` less for the enemy, until [`GOAL_UNTIL`]; all 0
    /// for nothing (v029). Band cells are those within [`GOAL_BAND`] rings of
    /// the frontline.
    ///
    /// - [`GOAL`]: each band cell at least [`GOAL_MARGIN`] steps nearer the
    ///   side's active land than the enemy's (being near: 0 steps is v029's
    ///   tie rule, a strict nearness);
    /// - [`GOAL_OWNED`]: each band cell the side holds actively;
    /// - [`GOAL_GUARD`]: each band cell it holds that is one of its active
    ///   towers or next to one (a tower stops units below level 3);
    /// - [`GOAL_CHOKE`]: each middle choke it holds actively.
    pub const GOAL: i64 = 0;
    /// See [`GOAL`].
    pub const GOAL_MARGIN: u8 = 1;
    /// See [`GOAL`].
    pub const GOAL_OWNED: i64 = 4;
    /// See [`GOAL`].
    pub const GOAL_GUARD: i64 = 0;
    /// See [`GOAL`].
    pub const GOAL_CHOKE: i64 = 0;
    /// The last game turn at which the goal counts: 14 since E076 (10 in v030).
    pub const GOAL_UNTIL: u32 = 14;
    /// The band's width: cells within this many rings of the frontline.
    pub const GOAL_BAND: i64 = 2;

    /// The land a side's position decides (E076, the owner, 2026-11-20: a
    /// centre cell the enemy takes is lost to it and shrinks the land behind
    /// it): each cell of the map nearer to a side's active land than to the
    /// enemy's (in steps over valid cells, as `econ::distances`) counts this
    /// much for it, until game turn [`VORONOI_UNTIL`]; 0 for nothing (v030).
    pub const VORONOI: i64 = 0;
    /// See [`VORONOI`].
    pub const VORONOI_UNTIL: u32 = 14;

    /// [`VORONOI`] for `seat`: its weight times the cells nearer to `seat`'s
    /// active land less those nearer to the enemy's.
    pub fn voronoi(state: &State, seat: usize) -> i64 {
        if VORONOI == 0 || state.game_turn() > VORONOI_UNTIL {
            return 0;
        }
        let ours = crate::ice_and_fire_opening::econ::distances(state, state.active(seat));
        let theirs = crate::ice_and_fire_opening::econ::distances(state, state.active(1 - seat));
        let mut net = 0;
        for c in state.map().valid.iter() {
            match ours[c].cmp(&theirs[c]) {
                std::cmp::Ordering::Less => net += 1,
                std::cmp::Ordering::Greater => net -= 1,
                std::cmp::Ordering::Equal => {}
            }
        }
        VORONOI * net
    }

    /// The map's band cells and middle chokes, computed once a map.
    struct GoalZones {
        valid: Bits,
        band: Bits,
        chokes: Bits,
    }

    thread_local! {
        static GOAL_ZONES: std::cell::RefCell<Option<GoalZones>> =
            const { std::cell::RefCell::new(None) };
    }

    /// The band cells and middle chokes of `state`'s map.
    pub fn goal_zones(state: &State) -> (Bits, Bits) {
        GOAL_ZONES.with(|cell| {
            let mut zones = cell.borrow_mut();
            let valid = state.map().valid;
            if zones.as_ref().is_none_or(|z| z.valid != valid) {
                let rings = crate::ice_and_fire_opening::solo::rings(state);
                let mut band = Bits::EMPTY;
                for c in valid.iter() {
                    if rings[c] <= GOAL_BAND {
                        band.set(c);
                    }
                }
                *zones = Some(GoalZones {
                    valid,
                    band,
                    chokes: crate::ice_and_fire_opening::solo::middle_chokes(state),
                });
            }
            zones
                .as_ref()
                .map_or((Bits::EMPTY, Bits::EMPTY), |z| (z.band, z.chokes))
        })
    }

    /// The cells of `seat` a tower guards: its active towers and their
    /// neighbours among its active cells.
    fn guarded(state: &State, seat: usize) -> Bits {
        let active = state.active(seat);
        let towers = state.towers() & active;
        (towers | towers.neighbours()) & active
    }

    /// The opening's goal for `seat` (E073), see [`GOAL`]; 0 after
    /// [`GOAL_UNTIL`].
    pub fn goal(state: &State, seat: usize) -> i64 {
        if (GOAL == 0 && GOAL_OWNED == 0 && GOAL_GUARD == 0 && GOAL_CHOKE == 0)
            || state.game_turn() > GOAL_UNTIL
        {
            return 0;
        }
        let (band, chokes) = goal_zones(state);
        let mut total = 0;
        if GOAL != 0 {
            let ours = crate::ice_and_fire_opening::econ::distances(state, state.active(seat));
            let theirs =
                crate::ice_and_fire_opening::econ::distances(state, state.active(1 - seat));
            let mut net = 0;
            for c in band.iter() {
                let (a, b) = (ours[c], theirs[c]);
                if a != u8::MAX && a.saturating_add(GOAL_MARGIN) <= b {
                    net += 1;
                } else if b != u8::MAX && b.saturating_add(GOAL_MARGIN) <= a {
                    net -= 1;
                }
            }
            total += GOAL * net;
        }
        let count = |bits: Bits| i64::from(bits.count());
        let (mine, theirs) = (state.active(seat), state.active(1 - seat));
        total += GOAL_OWNED * (count(mine & band) - count(theirs & band));
        if GOAL_GUARD != 0 {
            total += GOAL_GUARD
                * (count(guarded(state, seat) & band) - count(guarded(state, 1 - seat) & band));
        }
        total += GOAL_CHOKE * (count(mine & chokes) - count(theirs & chokes));
        total
    }

    /// The flanks (E095): the cells this many columns or more off the diagonal
    /// between the HQs, (0, 0) to (11, 11), on either side of it: toward
    /// (11, 0) for the first flank, toward (0, 11) for the second.
    pub const FLANK_OFF: i64 = 4;
    /// Each active cell of a side on its weaker flank (the flank where it holds
    /// fewer), up to [`FLANK_CAP`], counts this much for it, net of the enemy's,
    /// until game turn [`FLANK_UNTIL`]; 0 for nothing (v032, v033: E095's
    /// screening, 4 −5.6, 8 −15.6 and 16 −37.1 Elo).
    pub const FLANK: i64 = 0;
    /// See [`FLANK`].
    pub const FLANK_CAP: i64 = 4;
    /// See [`FLANK`].
    pub const FLANK_UNTIL: u32 = 12;

    /// The two flanks of [`FLANK_OFF`], as cells of the board, computed once.
    pub fn flanks() -> [Bits; 2] {
        static FLANKS: std::sync::OnceLock<[Bits; 2]> = std::sync::OnceLock::new();
        *FLANKS.get_or_init(flanks_of)
    }

    /// [`flanks`], computed.
    fn flanks_of() -> [Bits; 2] {
        let mut out = [Bits::EMPTY; 2];
        for c in 0..CELLS {
            let (x, y) = ((c % SIZE) as i64, (c / SIZE) as i64);
            if x - y >= FLANK_OFF {
                out[0].set(c);
            } else if y - x >= FLANK_OFF {
                out[1].set(c);
            }
        }
        out
    }

    /// The active cells of `seat` on its weaker flank, at most [`FLANK_CAP`].
    pub fn weaker_flank(state: &State, seat: usize) -> i64 {
        let [a, b] = flanks();
        let active = state.active(seat);
        i64::from((active & a).count().min((active & b).count())).min(FLANK_CAP)
    }

    /// [`FLANK`] for `seat`: its weight times our [`weaker_flank`] less the
    /// enemy's; 0 after [`FLANK_UNTIL`].
    pub fn flank(state: &State, seat: usize) -> i64 {
        if FLANK == 0 || state.game_turn() > FLANK_UNTIL {
            return 0;
        }
        FLANK * (weaker_flank(state, seat) - weaker_flank(state, 1 - seat))
    }

    /// The number of terms of the score that [`WEIGHTS`] weighs.
    pub const TERMS: usize = 17;

    /// The weight of each term of the score, in percent (E116): 100 is the
    /// evaluation as it was, `term * weight / 100` what a term counts. In order,
    /// each term being ours less theirs: the shared evaluation's five parts of
    /// material (`crate::ice_and_fire_tactics::eval::side_parts`): gold, 3 × income,
    /// 4 × active cells, units by training cost, 10 × active towers; its
    /// pressure term; the standing threat ([`standing`]); the debt of a side
    /// that cannot pay its upkeep, twice; [`shape`]; [`strong_units`]; the idle
    /// units ([`idle`]); the threatened cells (`THREAT_QUARTERS * threats / 4`);
    /// the [`mines`]; the [`wall`]; the [`goal`]; the [`voronoi`] term; the
    /// [`flank`] term. The threat of losing the HQ (`-WIN / 2`) and the finished
    /// games are not weighed. A quarter of the way from 100 to the weights
    /// fitted on the outcomes of 4,798 games of v034 against itself (E116): the
    /// fit itself lost, a quarter, a half and three quarters of the way won.
    pub const WEIGHTS: [i64; TERMS] = [
        82, 110, 124, 86, 81, 97, 123, 92, 96, 107, 126, 121, 109, 88, 100, 100, 100,
    ];

    /// `term` at `weight` percent.
    fn scaled(term: i64, weight: i64) -> i64 {
        if weight == 100 {
            term
        } else {
            term * weight / 100
        }
    }

    /// The score of `state` for `seat`, higher is better for it.
    pub fn eval(state: &State, seat: usize) -> i64 {
        eval_with(state, seat, &WEIGHTS)
    }

    /// [`eval`] with the term weights `w` rather than [`WEIGHTS`].
    #[inline(always)]
    pub fn eval_with(state: &State, seat: usize, w: &[i64; TERMS]) -> i64 {
        let movers = [
            movers_from(state, seat, MARGIN_MOVER_LEVEL),
            movers_from(state, 1 - seat, MARGIN_MOVER_LEVEL),
        ];
        let (score, margins) = evaluate_with_movers(state, seat, movers);
        let standing_diff = standing(margins[0]) - standing(margins[1]);
        if state.outcome().is_some() {
            return score + standing_diff;
        }
        let mut score = score + scaled(standing_diff, w[6]);
        if w[..6].iter().any(|&x| x != 100) {
            let ours = side_parts(state, seat);
            let theirs = side_parts(state, 1 - seat);
            for i in 0..5 {
                let part = ours[i] - theirs[i];
                score += scaled(part, w[i]) - part;
            }
            let press = pressure(margins[0]) - pressure(margins[1]);
            score += scaled(press, w[5]) - press;
        }
        let ours = exposed(state, seat);
        let theirs = exposed(state, 1 - seat);
        let threats = i64::from(theirs.count()) - i64::from(ours.count());
        score
            + scaled(-2 * debt(state, seat) + 2 * debt(state, 1 - seat), w[7])
            + scaled(shape(state, seat), w[8])
            + scaled(
                strong_units(state, seat) - strong_units(state, 1 - seat),
                w[9],
            )
            + scaled(-idle(state, seat) + idle(state, 1 - seat), w[10])
            + scaled(THREAT_QUARTERS * threats / 4, w[11])
            + scaled(
                mines(state, seat, ours) - mines(state, 1 - seat, theirs),
                w[12],
            )
            + scaled(wall(state, seat) - wall(state, 1 - seat), w[13])
            + scaled(goal(state, seat), w[14])
            + scaled(voronoi(state, seat), w[15])
            + scaled(flank(state, seat), w[16])
    }
}
mod search {
    //! The plan search (see the crate's docs): lethal first, then the opening
    //! until the middle game, then hill climbing over actions against a memory
    //! of the opponent's replies.
    //!
    //! A climb starts from the state at the start of the turn and adds, one at a
    //! time, the action that raises the score of the plan most. Trying every
    //! action at every step would cost too much for 10 to 40 ms, so a step is
    //! lazy: the actions are tried in the order of the gain each had when last
    //! tried (new ones first), and the step stops at the first whose old gain is
    //! no more than the best gain found in this step. When a lazy step finds no
    //! gain, one full pass tries the actions it skipped, so a climb ends on a
    //! plan that no single action improves. A later climb starts from the best
    //! gains the actions had in the earlier ones, since its first steps resemble
    //! theirs.
    //!
    //! When a climb has nothing new to learn (it found a plan found before, or
    //! the opponent's replies to its plan are in the memory already), the next
    //! climb may not start with the first action of any plan found so far
    //! (E014), so the climbs keep finding other plans until the time is up.
    //!
    //! When no first action left improves the plan, so that a climb ends on an
    //! empty plan, the time left goes to climbs forced to start with each of the
    //! root's other actions in turn, the best gain first (E029): an action that
    //! does not pay alone can open a plan that does.
    //!
    //! Each plan keeps the opponent's replies found for it (E027): the shared
    //! memory holds only the most damaging replies over all plans, so a plan's
    //! own worst reply could leave it. A plan's final score is the worst over the
    //! memory and its own replies, and the plan played must have had its replies
    //! searched: a plan found as the time ran out gets them in the time left
    //! before the hard limit, and if it then scores lower, the next best is
    //! checked in turn.

    use std::collections::hash_map::DefaultHasher;
    use std::collections::HashMap;
    use std::hash::BuildHasherDefault;
    use std::time::{Duration, Instant};

    use crate::ice_and_fire_engine::state::BUILD_COST;
    use crate::ice_and_fire_engine::{Bits, Command, Outcome, State, HQ, SIZE};
    use crate::ice_and_fire_opening::planned::Planned;
    use crate::ice_and_fire_policy::greedy_turn;
    use crate::ice_and_fire_tactics::chain::{chain_to, cost_to, cost_to_moving, UNREACHABLE};
    use crate::ice_and_fire_tactics::cut::cuts;
    use crate::ice_and_fire_tactics::eval::WIN;

    use crate::actions::{generate, xy, Action, CUT_LENGTH};
    use crate::eval::eval;
    use crate::strategy::Guide;

    mod steer {
        //! The type-guided climb (E106, stage 2 of
        //! `games/ice-and-fire/research/codingame/2026-11-28-type-planner.md`):
        //! each unit of ours is offered only the moves of its type's likeliest
        //! kinds, tried in the tables' order.

        use crate::ice_and_fire_engine::{Command, State, SIZE};

        use crate::actions::Action;
        use crate::types::{likeliest, prior, Kind, Typing, KINDS};

        /// The typing of one step of a climb and the table's probabilities for each
        /// unit that can move in it.
        pub struct Steer {
            typing: Typing,
            /// For each movable unit: its id, its cell and the probabilities of its
            /// key.
            units: Vec<(u32, usize, [u8; KINDS])>,
        }

        impl Steer {
            /// The typing of the side to act in `state`, one per step.
            pub fn new(state: &State) -> Steer {
                let typing = Typing::new(state);
                let units = state
                    .movable_units()
                    .iter()
                    .filter_map(|cell| {
                        let (id, _) = state.unit_at(cell)?;
                        let key = typing.key(state, cell)?;
                        Some((id, cell, prior(&key)))
                    })
                    .collect();
                Steer { typing, units }
            }

            /// The kind of `action` and the probabilities of its unit's key, if it
            /// is a single move of a unit of the step.
            fn kind_of(&self, state: &State, action: &Action) -> Option<(Kind, [u8; KINDS])> {
                let Action::One(Command::Move { id, x, y }) = action else {
                    return None;
                };
                let &(_, from, p) = self.units.iter().find(|u| u.0 == *id)?;
                let to = usize::from(*y) * SIZE + usize::from(*x);
                Some((self.typing.kind(state, from, to), p))
            }

            /// The prior of `action`: that of its kind for a single move, 0 for any
            /// other action.
            pub fn prior(&self, state: &State, action: &Action) -> u8 {
                self.kind_of(state, action)
                    .map_or(0, |(kind, p)| p[kind as usize])
            }

            /// Removes from `actions` the single moves whose kind is not among the
            /// `k` likeliest of their unit's key; every other action stays.
            pub fn filter(&self, state: &State, k: usize, actions: &mut Vec<Action>) {
                actions.retain(|action| match self.kind_of(state, action) {
                    Some((kind, p)) => {
                        let order = likeliest(&p);
                        order.is_empty() || order.iter().take(k).any(|&top| top == kind)
                    }
                    None => true,
                });
            }
        }
    }

    use steer::Steer;

    /// How many times the caps below are multiplied: 1 at CodinGame's limits.
    /// A teacher (E117) thinks `THINK_SCALE` times longer and scales its caps
    /// with it, since at CodinGame's caps most of its turns end at a cap.
    const CAP_SCALE: usize = 1;
    /// Cells added to the opponent's cuts in its replies, beyond our own
    /// `CUT_LENGTH` (E117's teacher).
    const REPLY_CUT_EXTRA: usize = 0;
    /// A deeper teacher (E118, `research/codingame/2026-11-28-deep-teacher.md`):
    /// `Some(n)` makes the middle game's turn compare its `n` best plans, and the
    /// plan today's search would play, by what our next turn can do after each of
    /// the opponent's replies to them (a whole turn search of ours from the state
    /// after the reply, its score taken, and the worst reply counting), and play
    /// the best. `None`: today's search alone, as in every release. Offline only:
    /// a deep turn takes [`DEEP_MS`], far beyond CodinGame's limit.
    pub const DEEP: Option<usize> = None;
    /// A deep turn's budget in milliseconds at CodinGame's time scale, multiplied
    /// by `CG_TIME_SCALE` as the other budgets are (E118). Today's search keeps
    /// its own budget at the start of it; the deep step runs until this.
    pub const DEEP_MS: f64 = 2000.0;
    /// What a lean deep leaf is (E119).
    #[derive(Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
    pub enum Leaf {
        /// A whole turn search of ours from the state after the reply, with no
        /// deep step, its final score taken (E118's leaf).
        Think,
        /// One climb of ours from that state, with no reply search, its end
        /// scored by `value`: a cheap estimate of our next turn.
        Climb,
        /// E120: a whole turn search where the time left per leaf is at least
        /// [`MIN_THINK_US`] (scaled by the time scale), else, for that candidate,
        /// one climb per leaf as `Climb`.
        Fit,
    }

    /// A lean deep step (E119, E118 made small enough for CodinGame's limit).
    #[derive(Clone, Copy)]
    pub struct Lean {
        /// The part of the turn, in percent, that today's search gets: its
        /// climbs, its final choice and its check end there.
        pub share: u32,
        /// The candidates compared: today's choice and the best others by
        /// today's score.
        pub candidates: usize,
        /// The most damaging replies of each candidate searched: its own and the
        /// memory's, without repeats, the worst for the candidate first.
        pub replies: usize,
        /// What a leaf is.
        pub leaf: Leaf,
        /// E120: today's search keeps its whole limits (`share` is not used) and
        /// the deep step runs only in the time it leaves before the hard limit
        /// (with `CG_FIXED_ITERS`, in [`FREE_TRIES_PCT`]% more tries), only when
        /// it ended before its time limit, its tries or the climb cap. A
        /// `Think` leaf that would get less than [`MIN_THINK_US`] is skipped,
        /// and its candidate not compared.
        pub free: bool,
    }

    /// E120: the smallest time, in microseconds at CodinGame's time scale
    /// (multiplied by `CG_TIME_SCALE`), a `Think` leaf of a free-time deep step
    /// gets; with less, the leaf is skipped.
    const MIN_THINK_US: f64 = 1000.0;
    /// E120: with `CG_FIXED_ITERS`, the tries of a free-time deep step, in
    /// percent of the tries of today's search.
    const FREE_TRIES_PCT: u128 = 50;

    /// The lean deep step (E119): after today's search, which has `share`% of the
    /// turn, the candidates' leaves are searched one candidate after the other,
    /// today's choice first, each leaf with the time left divided by the leaves
    /// left, up to the turn's hard limit. A candidate with a leaf undone is not
    /// compared; with no other complete candidate, today's choice is played.
    /// `None`: today's search alone, as in every release before v035. v035
    /// (E120) runs it in free time only: 2 candidates, their 2 worst replies,
    /// a whole turn search of ours at each leaf, after today's search has
    /// stopped on its own.
    pub const LEAN_DEPTH: Option<Lean> = Some(Lean {
        share: 100,
        candidates: 2,
        replies: 2,
        leaf: Leaf::Think,
        free: true,
    });
    /// Replies kept in the memory.
    const MEMORY_CAP: usize = 8 * CAP_SCALE;
    /// The opponent's best cuts added to the memory after a climb.
    const REPLY_CUTS: usize = 3 * CAP_SCALE;
    /// Most climbs in one turn.
    const MAX_CLIMBS: usize = 32 * CAP_SCALE;
    /// Most plans scored by the opponent's climb in one reply search (E019).
    const REPLY_EVALS: u64 = 300 * CAP_SCALE as u64;
    /// Where between the soft and the hard limit the middle game's climbs stop
    /// (E027): at 36 ms of a 40 ms turn rather than 24; the rest is for the
    /// final choice and its check.
    const CLIMB_SHARE: f64 = 0.75;

    /// The game turn from which the search plays whatever the opening would do
    /// (E067): `None` for never (v026, where the opening plays until we can
    /// pay a chain of trainings to an enemy cell).
    pub const HANDOVER_TURN: Option<u32> = Some(7);
    /// Whether the search also takes over, for good, at the first turn the
    /// opening would buy nothing while we hold [`HANDOVER_GOLD`] or more, from
    /// game turn [`HANDOVER_IDLE_FROM`] (E067).
    pub const HANDOVER_IDLE: bool = false;
    /// The gold of a level-1 training.
    pub const HANDOVER_GOLD: i64 = 10;
    pub const HANDOVER_IDLE_FROM: u32 = 6;

    /// The number of the likeliest kinds of action (`types::Kind`, by the
    /// table of zasmu's games for the unit's key) whose moves our own climbs
    /// offer a unit (E106, stage 2 of
    /// `research/codingame/2026-11-28-type-planner.md`); a move of another kind
    /// is not offered. `None`: none removed. Trainings, buildings and macro
    /// actions are never removed, and the opponent's model is never pruned.
    pub const TYPE_KINDS: Option<usize> = None;
    /// Whether our climbs break ties of the last gain by the table's prior (E106):
    /// moves by their kind's prior, highest first, then the other actions in the
    /// order generated. `false`: the order generated.
    pub const TYPE_ORDER: bool = false;
    /// The game turn from which [`TYPE_KINDS`] and [`TYPE_ORDER`] apply, by the
    /// game turn of a climb's root (E106).
    pub const TYPE_FROM_TURN: u32 = 7;

    /// When the search stops.
    #[derive(Clone, Copy)]
    pub struct Limit {
        /// No new climb, reply search or plan scoring starts after this, and a
        /// climb stops at its next try.
        pub soft: Option<Instant>,
        /// The choice among the plans stops scoring more of them after this.
        pub hard: Option<Instant>,
        /// Where a deep turn ends (E118): the deep step, which follows today's
        /// search, stops at this. Only used with [`DEEP`].
        pub deep: Option<Instant>,
        /// Most plans scored (one try of an action is one) during the climbs. The
        /// tests use it in place of a deadline, so that they are deterministic.
        pub max_evals: u64,
    }

    /// What the search decided.
    #[derive(Default)]
    pub struct Thought {
        /// The commands to send, each accepted in order on the state searched.
        pub commands: Vec<Command>,
        /// Climbs started.
        pub climbs: usize,
        /// Plans scored during the climbs (actions tried).
        pub evals: u64,
        /// Replies in the memory at the end.
        pub memory: usize,
        /// Different plans found by the climbs.
        pub plans: usize,
        /// Plans whose replies were searched only for the final choice (E027).
        pub checks: usize,
        /// Whether the climbs ran out of first actions and were then forced to
        /// start with each of the others (E029).
        pub forced: usize,
        /// The final score of the plan played, when the search chose among plans
        /// (E118: a leaf's value); `WIN` for a lethal turn.
        pub score: Option<i64>,
        /// Whether the opening played the turn.
        pub opening: bool,
        /// Whether the plan played starts with the strategic turn (E077).
        pub strategic: bool,
        /// The strategic turn's pieces the plan played holds (E077).
        pub pieces: usize,
    }

    /// Whether the plan played must have had its own replies searched (E027).
    const VERIFY: bool = true;

    /// One opponent reply: commands, each kept only if the rules accept it, and
    /// how much it hurt the plan it was found for (the evaluation after it, from
    /// our seat), lower being worse for us.
    #[derive(Clone)]
    struct Reply {
        commands: Vec<Command>,
        damage: i64,
    }

    /// A plan: the commands and the state after them.
    struct Plan {
        commands: Vec<Command>,
        end: State,
        /// The key of its first action, if any.
        first: Option<u64>,
        /// The opponent's replies to this plan, once searched (E027).
        own: Option<Vec<Reply>>,
    }

    /// The gain an action had when last tried, by [`key`].
    type Gains = HashMap<u64, i64, BuildHasherDefault<DefaultHasher>>;

    struct Search {
        me: usize,
        /// Whether this is the opponent's model, which the type switches never
        /// touch (E106).
        opponent: bool,
        limit: Limit,
        evals: u64,
        /// The best gain each action ever had in an earlier climb: where a new
        /// climb tries the actions first, since the first steps of a climb
        /// resemble those of the one before.
        hints: Gains,
        /// The actions of the climbs' root, generated once: every climb of a
        /// search starts from the same state.
        root_actions: Option<Vec<Action>>,
        /// Whether the strike reserve holds this turn (E069).
        strike: bool,
        /// The strategic layer's guide this turn (E077): its plan and the
        /// objectives' term.
        guide: Option<Guide>,
        /// The deep step's candidates and leaves (E118).
        deep_stats: (usize, usize),
    }

    /// The strike reserve (E069, stage B of the curriculum in
    /// `research/codingame/2026-11-18-zasmu-strategy.md`): when, at the start of
    /// the turn, no strike of the opponent's threatens our HQ and our chain of
    /// trainings to the enemy HQ (all our units stepping first) is affordable
    /// with our gold plus this many turns of income, the search plays no plan
    /// that leaves it unaffordable within as many turns. 0 for none (v028,
    /// v029); 1 was the probe of E069.
    pub const STRIKE_TURNS: i64 = 0;

    /// The blockers offered (E044): towers on our cells that the opponent's
    /// remembered replies enter. Towers alone won the screening.
    pub const BLOCK_TOWERS: bool = true;
    /// Towers also on our free cells next to those cells (a tower guards its
    /// neighbours).
    pub const BLOCK_NEIGHBOURS: bool = false;
    /// A training at this level on those cells when they are empty (`None`:
    /// none).
    pub const BLOCK_LEVEL: Option<u8> = None;

    /// Adds to `out` the blockers of the replies of `memory` (E044), as
    /// [`BLOCK_TOWERS`], [`BLOCK_NEIGHBOURS`] and [`BLOCK_LEVEL`] say.
    fn blockers(state: &State, memory: &[Reply], out: &mut Vec<Action>) {
        if !BLOCK_TOWERS && BLOCK_LEVEL.is_none() {
            return;
        }
        let replies = memory.iter().map(|reply| reply.commands.as_slice());
        blockers_of(
            state,
            replies,
            (BLOCK_TOWERS, BLOCK_NEIGHBOURS, BLOCK_LEVEL),
            out,
        );
    }

    /// Adds to `out` the blockers of the cells of the player to act in `state`
    /// that `replies` enter by a training or a move (E044): with `towers`,
    /// towers on them (and with `neighbours`, on our free cells next to them);
    /// with a `level`, a training at that level on those that are empty; each
    /// unless `out` holds the same action already.
    pub(crate) fn blockers_of<'a>(
        state: &State,
        replies: impl Iterator<Item = &'a [Command]>,
        (towers, neighbours, level): (bool, bool, Option<u8>),
        out: &mut Vec<Action>,
    ) {
        let me = state.to_act();
        let mine = state.active(me);
        let mut entered = Bits::EMPTY;
        for reply in replies {
            for command in reply {
                if let Command::Train { x, y, .. } | Command::Move { x, y, .. } = *command {
                    let cell = usize::from(y) * SIZE + usize::from(x);
                    if mine.test(cell) {
                        entered |= Bits::cell(cell);
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        if entered.is_empty() {
            return;
        }
        let free = state.empty_cells() & mine;
        let gold = state.gold(me);
        let push = |command: Command, out: &mut Vec<Action>| {
            if !out.iter().any(|a| a.commands() == [command]) {
                out.push(Action::One(command));
            }
        };
        if towers && gold >= BUILD_COST && state.league().allows_towers() {
            let mut cells = entered;
            if neighbours {
                cells |= entered.neighbours();
            }
            for cell in (cells & free).and_not(state.map().spots).iter() {
                let (x, y) = xy(cell);
                push(Command::BuildTower { x, y }, out);
            }
        }
        if let Some(level) = level.filter(|&level| level <= state.league().max_level()) {
            if gold >= 10 * i64::from(level) {
                for cell in (entered & free).iter() {
                    let (x, y) = xy(cell);
                    push(Command::Train { level, x, y }, out);
                }
            }
        }
    }

    /// Whether every command of `commands` is accepted in order by `state`.
    fn apply_all(state: &mut State, commands: &[Command]) -> bool {
        commands.iter().all(|&command| state.apply(command))
    }

    /// A key to remember an action by.
    fn key(commands: &[Command]) -> u64 {
        let mut hash: u64 = 0xcbf2_9ce4_8422_2325;
        for command in commands {
            let (kind, a, b, c) = match *command {
                Command::Move { id, x, y } => (1, u64::from(id), x, y),
                Command::Train { level, x, y } => (2, u64::from(level), x, y),
                Command::BuildMine { x, y } => (3, 0, x, y),
                Command::BuildTower { x, y } => (4, 0, x, y),
                Command::Wait => (5, 0, 0, 0),
            };
            let word = kind | a << 8 | u64::from(b) << 40 | u64::from(c) << 48;
            hash = (hash ^ word).wrapping_mul(0x0100_0000_01b3);
        }
        hash
    }

    /// The state after our plan `end`, the opponent's turn with `reply` and the
    /// start of ours.
    fn after_reply(end: &State, reply: &[Command]) -> State {
        let mut next = end.clone();
        next.end_turn();
        for &command in reply {
            next.apply(command);
        }
        next.end_turn();
        next
    }

    /// The plan, a lethal move or chain, that takes the enemy HQ now, if there is
    /// one.
    fn lethal(state: &State) -> Option<Vec<Command>> {
        let me = state.to_act();
        let target = HQ[1 - me];
        let wins = |trial: &State| trial.outcome() == Some(Outcome::Win(me));
        // A unit next to the HQ steps in.
        for cell in state.movable_units().iter() {
            if state.map().distance(cell, target) != 1 {
                continue;
            }
            let Some((id, _)) = state.unit_at(cell) else {
                continue;
            };
            let (x, y) = xy(target);
            let command = Command::Move { id, x, y };
            let mut trial = state.clone();
            if trial.apply(command) && wins(&trial) {
                return Some(vec![command]);
            }
        }
        let chain = chain_to(state, target, state.gold(me))?;
        let mut trial = state.clone();
        (apply_all(&mut trial, &chain.commands) && wins(&trial)).then_some(chain.commands)
    }

    /// Whether `seat`'s chain of trainings to the enemy HQ, all its units
    /// stepping first, is affordable in `state` with its gold plus `turns`
    /// turns of income (E069).
    pub(crate) fn strike_within(state: &State, seat: usize, turns: i64) -> bool {
        let cost = cost_to_moving(state, seat, state.units(seat), HQ[1 - seat]);
        cost != UNREACHABLE && state.gold(seat) + turns * state.income(seat) >= cost
    }

    /// Whether the strike reserve holds in `state`, the start of a turn of the
    /// player to act (E069): [`STRIKE_TURNS`] is not 0, the opponent cannot take
    /// our HQ at its next turn whatever we do, and our strike is affordable
    /// within [`STRIKE_TURNS`] turns.
    pub(crate) fn strike_reserve(state: &State) -> bool {
        let me = state.to_act();
        if STRIKE_TURNS == 0 || state.outcome().is_some() {
            return false;
        }
        let mut next = state.clone();
        next.end_turn();
        let threatened =
            next.outcome().is_none() && cost_to(&next, 1 - me, true, HQ[me]) <= next.gold(1 - me);
        !threatened && strike_within(state, me, STRIKE_TURNS)
    }

    impl Search {
        /// Whether the plan whose state is `end` breaks the strike reserve
        /// (E069): the reserve holds this turn, the plan does not win, and it
        /// leaves our strike unaffordable within [`STRIKE_TURNS`] turns.
        fn breaks_reserve(&self, end: &State) -> bool {
            self.strike
                && end.outcome() != Some(Outcome::Win(self.me))
                && !strike_within(end, self.me, STRIKE_TURNS)
        }

        /// Whether the climbs must stop.
        fn spent(&self) -> bool {
            self.evals >= self.limit.max_evals
                || self.limit.soft.is_some_and(|t| Instant::now() >= t)
        }

        /// The score of the plan whose state is `end` against `memory`: the worst
        /// evaluation after a reply, or the evaluation of `end` itself with an
        /// empty memory. The replies are tried most damaging first and the
        /// scoring stops once the score is no more than `bound`, so a result
        /// above `bound` is exact and any other is an upper bound.
        fn score(&mut self, end: &State, memory: &[Reply], bound: i64) -> i64 {
            self.evals += 1;
            self.rate(end, memory, bound)
        }

        fn rate(&self, end: &State, memory: &[Reply], bound: i64) -> i64 {
            if end.outcome() == Some(Outcome::Win(self.me)) {
                return WIN;
            }
            if memory.is_empty() {
                return self.value(end);
            }
            let mut worst = i64::MAX;
            for reply in memory {
                worst = worst.min(self.value(&after_reply(end, &reply.commands)));
                if worst <= bound {
                    break;
                }
            }
            worst
        }

        /// The evaluation of `state` for us, with the objectives' term of the
        /// guide (E077).
        fn value(&self, state: &State) -> i64 {
            let base = eval(state, self.me);
            match &self.guide {
                Some(guide) if state.outcome().is_none() => base + guide.term(state, self.me),
                _ => base,
            }
        }

        /// The typing of a step of a climb from `root`, when [`TYPE_KINDS`] or
        /// [`TYPE_ORDER`] apply to it (E106): ours only, from [`TYPE_FROM_TURN`].
        fn steer(&self, root: &State, cur: &State) -> Option<Steer> {
            let on = (TYPE_KINDS.is_some() || TYPE_ORDER)
                && !self.opponent
                && root.game_turn() >= TYPE_FROM_TURN;
            on.then(|| Steer::new(cur))
        }

        /// Adds the strategic turn's pieces to `actions` (E077).
        fn add_pieces(&self, actions: &mut Vec<Action>) {
            if let Some(guide) = &self.guide {
                for piece in &guide.pieces {
                    actions.push(Action::Many(piece.clone()));
                }
            }
        }

        /// One pass over `actions` in `order` from the plan state `cur`: the best
        /// action that scores above `cur_score`, with its state and score. With
        /// `lazy`, stops at the first action whose last gain is no more than the
        /// best gain so far, and says so in the second result. Actions with
        /// `done` set were tried in this step already.
        #[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]
        fn pass(
            &mut self,
            cur: &State,
            cur_score: i64,
            actions: &[Action],
            order: &[(i64, usize)],
            done: &mut [bool],
            memory: &[Reply],
            gains: &mut Gains,
            lazy: bool,
        ) -> (Option<(usize, State, i64)>, bool) {
            let mut best = None;
            let mut best_score = cur_score;
            for &(old, index) in order {
                if done[index] {
                    continue;
                }
                if lazy && old != i64::MAX && old <= best_score - cur_score {
                    return (best, true);
                }
                if self.spent() {
                    return (best, false);
                }
                done[index] = true;
                let commands = actions[index].commands();
                let mut next = cur.clone();
                if !apply_all(&mut next, commands) || self.breaks_reserve(&next) {
                    gains.insert(key(commands), i64::MIN / 4);
                    continue;
                }
                let score = self.score(&next, memory, best_score);
                gains.insert(key(commands), score - cur_score);
                if score > best_score {
                    best_score = score;
                    best = Some((index, next, score));
                }
            }
            (best, false)
        }

        /// One climb from `root` against `memory`, never starting with an
        /// action whose key is in `banned`. With `cached`, `root` is the
        /// search's root, whose actions are generated once.
        fn climb(&mut self, root: &State, memory: &[Reply], banned: &[u64], cached: bool) -> Plan {
            let mut first = None;
            let mut cur = root.clone();
            let mut commands = Vec::new();
            let mut cur_score = self.score(&cur, memory, i64::MIN);
            let mut gains = Gains::default();
            let mut actions = Vec::new();
            let mut order = Vec::new();
            while cur.outcome().is_none() && !self.spent() {
                if commands.is_empty() && cached {
                    match &self.root_actions {
                        Some(root_actions) => actions.clone_from(root_actions),
                        None => {
                            generate(&cur, &mut actions);
                            // The strategic turn as one macro action (E077).
                            if let Some(guide) = self.guide.as_ref().filter(|g| g.offered) {
                                actions.push(Action::Many(guide.plan.clone()));
                            }
                            self.add_pieces(&mut actions);
                            self.root_actions = Some(actions.clone());
                        }
                    }
                } else {
                    generate(&cur, &mut actions);
                    self.add_pieces(&mut actions);
                }
                blockers(&cur, memory, &mut actions);
                let steer = self.steer(root, &cur);
                if let (Some(steer), Some(k)) = (&steer, TYPE_KINDS) {
                    steer.filter(&cur, k, &mut actions);
                }
                order.clear();
                for (index, action) in actions.iter().enumerate() {
                    let k = key(action.commands());
                    let old = gains.get(&k).or(self.hints.get(&k)).copied();
                    order.push((old.unwrap_or(i64::MAX), index));
                }
                // Highest last gain first, new actions before all, then in the
                // order generated.
                // With [`TYPE_ORDER`], ties go by the prior (E106).
                match steer.as_ref().filter(|_| TYPE_ORDER) {
                    Some(steer) => {
                        let priors: Vec<u8> =
                            actions.iter().map(|a| steer.prior(&cur, a)).collect();
                        order.sort_by(|a, b| {
                            (b.0.cmp(&a.0))
                                .then(priors[b.1].cmp(&priors[a.1]))
                                .then(a.1.cmp(&b.1))
                        });
                    }
                    None => order.sort_by(|a, b| b.0.cmp(&a.0).then(a.1.cmp(&b.1))),
                }
                let mut done = vec![false; actions.len()];
                if commands.is_empty() {
                    for (index, action) in actions.iter().enumerate() {
                        done[index] = banned.contains(&key(action.commands()));
                    }
                }
                // A lazy pass, then a full one if the lazy one skipped actions
                // and found no gain.
                let mut best = None;
                for lazy in [true, false] {
                    let (found, skipped) = self.pass(
                        &cur, cur_score, &actions, &order, &mut done, memory, &mut gains, lazy,
                    );
                    best = found;
                    if best.is_some() || !skipped {
                        break;
                    }
                }
                let Some((index, next, score)) = best else {
                    break;
                };
                if commands.is_empty() {
                    first = Some(key(actions[index].commands()));
                }
                commands.extend_from_slice(actions[index].commands());
                cur = next;
                cur_score = score;
            }
            for (k, gain) in gains {
                let hint = self.hints.entry(k).or_insert(gain);
                *hint = (*hint).max(gain);
            }
            Plan {
                commands,
                end: cur,
                first,
                own: None,
            }
        }

        /// The replies of the opponent to the plan that ends in `end`: its
        /// lethal chain, its best cuts, bronze's greedy turn and its own plan
        /// (one climb), on the state after our turn ends.
        fn replies(&self, end: &State) -> Vec<Vec<Command>> {
            let mut next = end.clone();
            next.end_turn();
            let mut out = Vec::new();
            if next.outcome().is_some() {
                return out;
            }
            let opponent = next.to_act();
            let gold = next.gold(opponent);
            if let Some(chain) = chain_to(&next, HQ[self.me], gold) {
                out.push(chain.commands);
            }
            for cut in cuts(&next, CUT_LENGTH + REPLY_CUT_EXTRA, gold, REPLY_CUTS) {
                out.push(cut.commands);
            }
            let mut greedy = Vec::new();
            greedy_turn(&next, &mut greedy);
            out.push(greedy);
            // The opponent's own plan (E019): a climb from its seat, with moves,
            // trainings and cuts, scored by the evaluation from its side.
            let mut theirs = Search {
                me: opponent,
                opponent: true,
                limit: Limit {
                    max_evals: REPLY_EVALS,
                    ..self.limit
                },
                evals: 0,
                hints: Gains::default(),
                root_actions: None,
                // The opponent's model keeps no reserve, as before E069.
                strike: false,
                guide: None,
                deep_stats: (0, 0),
            };
            out.push(theirs.climb(&next, &[], &[], true).commands);
            out.retain(|commands| !commands.is_empty());
            out
        }

        /// The replies to the plan that ends in `end`, each with its damage.
        fn answers(&self, end: &State) -> Vec<Reply> {
            self.replies(end)
                .into_iter()
                .map(|commands| {
                    let damage = self.value(&after_reply(end, &commands));
                    Reply { commands, damage }
                })
                .collect()
        }

        /// A climb from `root` forced to start with `action` (E029), or `None`
        /// when the rules refuse it.
        fn forced(&mut self, root: &State, action: &Action, memory: &[Reply]) -> Option<Plan> {
            let mut after = root.clone();
            if !apply_all(&mut after, action.commands()) || self.breaks_reserve(&after) {
                return None;
            }
            self.evals += 1;
            let rest = self.climb(&after, memory, &[], false);
            let mut commands = action.commands().to_vec();
            commands.extend_from_slice(&rest.commands);
            Some(Plan {
                commands,
                end: rest.end,
                first: Some(key(action.commands())),
                own: None,
            })
        }

        /// The score of `plan` for the final choice: the worst over `memory` and
        /// the plan's own replies (E027).
        fn final_score(&self, plan: &Plan, memory: &[Reply]) -> i64 {
            let score = self.rate(&plan.end, memory, i64::MIN);
            match &plan.own {
                Some(own) if !own.is_empty() => score.min(self.rate(&plan.end, own, i64::MIN)),
                _ => score,
            }
        }
    }

    impl Search {
        /// The deep step (E118): the index of the plan to play among `plans`
        /// (scored `scores`, today's choice `today`), compared by what our next
        /// turn can do. The candidates are the `width` best plans and today's; a
        /// candidate's score is the worst over its replies (the memory's and its
        /// own) of the final score of the plan a whole turn search of ours plays
        /// from the state after the reply. The searches share the time to
        /// `limit.deep` evenly, or the tries when there is no clock. On a tie
        /// today's choice wins, then the earlier candidate.
        fn deepen(
            &mut self,
            plans: &[Plan],
            scores: &[Option<i64>],
            memory: &[Reply],
            (today, width): (Option<usize>, usize),
            limit: Limit,
            opening: &mut Planned,
        ) -> Option<usize> {
            let today = today?;
            let score_of = |index: usize| scores[index].unwrap_or(i64::MIN);
            // The best first, the earlier on a tie.
            let mut order: Vec<usize> = (0..plans.len()).collect();
            order.sort_by_key(|&index| std::cmp::Reverse(score_of(index)));
            let mut candidates: Vec<usize> = order.into_iter().take(width).collect();
            if !candidates.contains(&today) {
                candidates.push(today);
            }
            // Each candidate's leaves: the states after its replies.
            let mut leaves: Vec<Vec<State>> = Vec::new();
            for &index in &candidates {
                let plan = &plans[index];
                let mut states = Vec::new();
                if plan.end.outcome().is_none() {
                    let mut seen: Vec<&[Command]> = Vec::new();
                    let own = plan.own.iter().flatten();
                    for reply in memory.iter().chain(own) {
                        if !seen.contains(&reply.commands.as_slice()) {
                            seen.push(&reply.commands);
                            states.push(after_reply(&plan.end, &reply.commands));
                        }
                    }
                }
                leaves.push(states);
            }
            let total: usize = leaves.iter().map(Vec::len).sum();
            self.deep_stats = (candidates.len(), total);
            let mut left = total;
            let mut best: Option<(i64, bool, usize)> = None;
            for (rank, &index) in candidates.iter().enumerate() {
                // A plan with no replies to search keeps its final score.
                let mut deep = if leaves[rank].is_empty() {
                    self.final_score(&plans[index], memory)
                } else {
                    i64::MAX
                };
                for leaf in &leaves[rank] {
                    let value = self.leaf_value(leaf, limit, left, opening);
                    left -= 1;
                    deep = deep.min(value);
                }
                let key = (deep, index == today, std::cmp::Reverse(rank));
                let better = best.is_none_or(|(d, t, r)| key > (d, t, std::cmp::Reverse(r)));
                if better {
                    best = Some((deep, index == today, rank));
                }
            }
            best.map(|(_, _, rank)| candidates[rank])
        }

        /// The value of the leaf `state`, the start of our next turn: the final
        /// score of the plan a turn search of ours plays from it, within an even
        /// share of the deep time (or tries) left for the `left` leaves not yet
        /// searched.
        fn leaf_value(
            &self,
            state: &State,
            limit: Limit,
            left: usize,
            opening: &mut Planned,
        ) -> i64 {
            if state.outcome().is_some() {
                return self.value(state);
            }
            let share = left.max(1);
            let leaf_limit = match limit.deep {
                Some(deep) => {
                    let now = Instant::now();
                    let room = deep.saturating_duration_since(now).div_f64(share as f64);
                    Limit {
                        soft: Some(now + room.mul_f64(0.6)),
                        hard: Some(now + room),
                        deep: None,
                        max_evals: u64::MAX,
                    }
                }
                None => Limit {
                    soft: None,
                    hard: None,
                    deep: None,
                    max_evals: (limit.max_evals / share as u64).max(1),
                },
            };
            let thought = think_in(state, leaf_limit, opening, None, (None, None));
            thought.score.unwrap_or_else(|| self.value(state))
        }
    }

    /// `limit` with its clock and its tries cut to `share`% of what is left.
    fn lean_limit(limit: Limit, share: u32) -> Limit {
        let now = Instant::now();
        let part = f64::from(share) / 100.0;
        let cut = |t: Instant| now + t.saturating_duration_since(now).mul_f64(part);
        Limit {
            soft: limit.soft.map(cut),
            hard: limit.hard.map(cut),
            deep: None,
            max_evals: (u128::from(limit.max_evals) * u128::from(share) / 100).max(1) as u64,
        }
    }

    impl Search {
        /// The lean deep step (E119): the index of the plan to play among
        /// `plans`, or `None` to keep today's choice. The candidates are today's
        /// choice, then the best scored others, `lean.candidates` in all. A
        /// candidate's leaves are the states after its `lean.replies` most
        /// damaging replies (the memory's and its own, by the evaluation after
        /// each from our seat); its deep score is the worst leaf, and only a
        /// candidate with all its leaves done is compared. The leaves share the
        /// time to `full.hard` evenly, each taking the time left divided by the
        /// leaves left; with no clock, the tries `full` keeps beyond today's
        /// share, in the same proportions. On a tie today's choice wins, then the
        /// earlier candidate.
        fn lean_step(
            &self,
            plans: &[Plan],
            scores: &[Option<i64>],
            memory: &[Reply],
            (today, lean): (Option<usize>, Lean),
            (full, opening): (Limit, &mut Planned),
        ) -> Option<usize> {
            let today = today?;
            // The leaf's kind, read from the switch.
            let kind = if lean.leaf == Leaf::Climb {
                Leaf::Climb
            } else {
                Leaf::Think
            };
            let mut order: Vec<usize> = (0..plans.len())
                .filter(|&index| index != today && scores[index].is_some())
                .collect();
            order.sort_by_key(|&index| std::cmp::Reverse(scores[index]));
            let candidates: Vec<usize> = std::iter::once(today)
                .chain(order)
                .take(lean.candidates.max(1))
                .collect();
            // Each candidate's leaves, the worst for it first.
            let mut leaves: Vec<Vec<State>> = Vec::new();
            for &index in &candidates {
                let plan = &plans[index];
                let mut rated: Vec<(i64, State)> = Vec::new();
                if plan.end.outcome().is_none() {
                    let mut seen: Vec<&[Command]> = Vec::new();
                    let own = plan.own.iter().flatten();
                    for reply in memory.iter().chain(own) {
                        if !seen.contains(&reply.commands.as_slice()) {
                            seen.push(&reply.commands);
                            let after = after_reply(&plan.end, &reply.commands);
                            rated.push((self.value(&after), after));
                        }
                    }
                }
                // Stable: the memory's order on a tie.
                rated.sort_by_key(|(damage, _)| *damage);
                rated.truncate(lean.replies.max(1));
                leaves.push(rated.into_iter().map(|(_, after)| after).collect());
            }
            let total: usize = leaves.iter().map(Vec::len).sum();
            let tries = if lean.free {
                u128::from(full.max_evals) * FREE_TRIES_PCT / 100
            } else {
                u128::from(full.max_evals) * u128::from(100 - lean.share.min(100)) / 100
            };
            let min_think =
                Duration::from_secs_f64(MIN_THINK_US / 1e6 * crate::cg_core::time::time_scale());
            let each = (tries / total.max(1) as u128).max(1) as u64;
            let mut left = total;
            let mut best: Option<(i64, bool, usize)> = None;
            for (rank, &index) in candidates.iter().enumerate() {
                let mut deep = if leaves[rank].is_empty() {
                    self.final_score(&plans[index], memory)
                } else {
                    i64::MAX
                };
                // Whether the time left gives each leaf a whole turn search
                // (E120, free time only).
                let fits = |left: usize| match full.hard {
                    Some(hard) if lean.free => {
                        hard.saturating_duration_since(Instant::now())
                            .div_f64(left.max(1) as f64)
                            >= min_think
                    }
                    _ => true,
                };
                let mut kind = kind;
                let mut complete = true;
                if lean.free && kind == Leaf::Think && !leaves[rank].is_empty() && !fits(left) {
                    if lean.leaf == Leaf::Fit {
                        kind = Leaf::Climb;
                    } else {
                        left -= leaves[rank].len();
                        continue;
                    }
                }
                for leaf in &leaves[rank] {
                    if full.hard.is_some_and(|hard| Instant::now() >= hard) {
                        return best.map(|(_, _, rank)| candidates[rank]);
                    }
                    if kind == Leaf::Think && !fits(left) {
                        complete = false;
                        left -= 1;
                        continue;
                    }
                    let mut leaf_limit = Limit {
                        soft: None,
                        hard: None,
                        deep: None,
                        max_evals: each,
                    };
                    if let Some(hard) = full.hard {
                        let now = Instant::now();
                        let room = hard
                            .saturating_duration_since(now)
                            .div_f64(left.max(1) as f64);
                        let soft = if kind == Leaf::Think { 0.6 } else { 0.9 };
                        leaf_limit.soft = Some(now + room.mul_f64(soft));
                        leaf_limit.hard = Some(now + room);
                        leaf_limit.max_evals = u64::MAX;
                    }
                    let value = self.lean_leaf(leaf, kind, leaf_limit, opening);
                    left -= 1;
                    deep = deep.min(value);
                }
                if !complete {
                    continue;
                }
                let key = (deep, index == today, std::cmp::Reverse(rank));
                let better = best.is_none_or(|(d, t, r)| key > (d, t, std::cmp::Reverse(r)));
                if better {
                    best = Some((deep, index == today, rank));
                }
            }
            best.map(|(_, _, rank)| candidates[rank])
        }

        /// The value of the leaf `state`, the start of our next turn, within
        /// `limit`.
        fn lean_leaf(&self, state: &State, kind: Leaf, limit: Limit, opening: &mut Planned) -> i64 {
            if state.outcome().is_some() {
                return self.value(state);
            }
            match kind {
                Leaf::Think => {
                    let thought = think_in(state, limit, opening, None, (None, None));
                    thought.score.unwrap_or_else(|| self.value(state))
                }
                Leaf::Climb | Leaf::Fit => {
                    if lethal(state).is_some() {
                        return WIN;
                    }
                    let mut search = Search {
                        me: self.me,
                        opponent: false,
                        limit,
                        evals: 0,
                        hints: Gains::default(),
                        root_actions: None,
                        strike: strike_reserve(state),
                        guide: None,
                        deep_stats: (0, 0),
                    };
                    let plan = search.climb(state, &[], &[], true);
                    search.rate(&plan.end, &[], i64::MIN)
                }
            }
        }
    }

    /// Adds the replies `found` that the memory does not hold, then keeps the
    /// [`MEMORY_CAP`] most damaging. Whether the memory changed.
    fn remember(found: &[Reply], memory: &mut Vec<Reply>) -> bool {
        let before: Vec<_> = memory.iter().map(|r| r.commands.clone()).collect();
        for reply in found {
            if memory.iter().any(|r| r.commands == reply.commands) {
                continue;
            }
            memory.push(reply.clone());
        }
        // Stable: the older reply stays first on a tie.
        memory.sort_by_key(|reply| reply.damage);
        memory.truncate(MEMORY_CAP);
        memory.iter().map(|r| &r.commands).ne(&before)
    }

    /// The commands to play in `state` for the player to act, within `limit`;
    /// `opening` plays until the middle game (`crate::ice_and_fire_opening::middle`).
    pub fn think(state: &State, limit: Limit, opening: &mut Planned) -> Thought {
        think_with(state, limit, opening, None)
    }

    /// [`think`] with the strategic layer's guide for the turn (E077): its plan
    /// offered as a macro action or as the first climb's start, and the
    /// objectives' term added to the score.
    pub fn think_with(
        state: &State,
        limit: Limit,
        opening: &mut Planned,
        guide: Option<Guide>,
    ) -> Thought {
        think_in(state, limit, opening, guide, (DEEP, LEAN_DEPTH))
    }

    /// [`think_with`] with the deep step's width: `deep` is [`DEEP`] for a turn
    /// and `None` inside the deep step's own searches (E118), never recursive.
    fn think_in(
        state: &State,
        limit: Limit,
        opening: &mut Planned,
        guide: Option<Guide>,
        (deep, lean): (Option<usize>, Option<Lean>),
    ) -> Thought {
        let me = state.to_act();
        let mut thought = Thought::default();
        if state.outcome().is_some() {
            return thought;
        }
        if let Some(commands) = lethal(state) {
            thought.commands = commands;
            thought.score = Some(WIN);
            return thought;
        }
        // A time between the soft and the hard limit.
        let at = |share: f64| match (limit.soft, limit.hard) {
            (Some(soft), Some(hard)) => Some(soft + (hard - soft).mul_f64(share)),
            _ => None,
        };
        if HANDOVER_TURN.is_some_and(|turn| state.game_turn() >= turn) {
            opening.end();
        }
        if opening.playing(state) {
            // The opening's choice stops at 76% of the turn: the hard limit is
            // the whole budget.
            let commands = opening.turn(state, at(0.4));
            let buys = commands.iter().any(|command| {
                matches!(
                    command,
                    Command::Train { .. } | Command::BuildMine { .. } | Command::BuildTower { .. }
                )
            });
            let idle = HANDOVER_IDLE
                && !buys
                && state.game_turn() >= HANDOVER_IDLE_FROM
                && state.gold(me) >= HANDOVER_GOLD;
            if !idle {
                thought.opening = true;
                thought.commands = commands;
                return thought;
            }
            // The opening would keep its gold: the search plays from here on.
            opening.end();
        }
        // A lean deep turn (E119) gives today's search a share of the turn.
        let full = limit;
        // A free-time one (E120) leaves today's search all of it.
        let limit = lean
            .filter(|lean| !lean.free)
            .map_or(limit, |lean| lean_limit(limit, lean.share));
        let at = |share: f64| match (limit.soft, limit.hard) {
            (Some(soft), Some(hard)) => Some(soft + (hard - soft).mul_f64(share)),
            _ => None,
        };
        let mut search = Search {
            me,
            opponent: false,
            limit: Limit {
                soft: at(CLIMB_SHARE),
                ..limit
            },
            evals: 0,
            hints: Gains::default(),
            root_actions: None,
            strike: strike_reserve(state),
            guide,
            deep_stats: (0, 0),
        };
        let mut memory = Vec::new();
        let mut plans: Vec<Plan> = Vec::new();
        let mut banned = Vec::new();
        // Set when no first action left improves the plan (E029).
        let mut exhausted = false;
        let mut forced: Vec<Action> = Vec::new();
        // The first climb starts with the strategic turn (E077).
        let mut start = search
            .guide
            .as_ref()
            .filter(|g| g.start)
            .map(|g| Action::Many(g.plan.clone()));
        while thought.climbs < MAX_CLIMBS && (plans.is_empty() || !search.spent()) {
            let started = match start.take() {
                Some(action) => search.forced(state, &action, &memory),
                None => None,
            };
            let plan = if let Some(plan) = started {
                plan
            } else if exhausted {
                let Some(action) = forced.pop() else {
                    break;
                };
                match search.forced(state, &action, &memory) {
                    Some(plan) => plan,
                    None => continue,
                }
            } else {
                search.climb(state, &memory, &banned, true)
            };
            thought.climbs += 1;
            // A climb that ends on a plan found before has nothing new to learn.
            let same = plans.iter().any(|p| p.commands == plan.commands);
            let first = plan.first;
            // Out of time, the plan is kept and no reply searched yet.
            let stop = search.spent();
            let mut plan = plan;
            let mut more = false;
            if !stop && !same {
                let found = search.answers(&plan.end);
                more = remember(&found, &mut memory);
                plan.own = Some(found);
            }
            if !same {
                plans.push(plan);
            }
            if stop {
                break;
            }
            // A climb against the same memory would find the same plan again:
            // the next one starts elsewhere (E014). When the plan was empty, no
            // first action left improves it: the next climbs are forced to start
            // with each of the others, the best gain so far first (E029).
            if !more && !exhausted {
                match first {
                    Some(first) => banned.push(first),
                    None => {
                        exhausted = true;
                        forced = search.root_actions.clone().unwrap_or_default();
                        forced.retain(|a| !banned.contains(&key(a.commands())));
                        let steer = search.steer(state, state);
                        if let (Some(steer), Some(k)) = (&steer, TYPE_KINDS) {
                            steer.filter(state, k, &mut forced);
                        }
                        let gain = |a: &Action| {
                            search
                                .hints
                                .get(&key(a.commands()))
                                .copied()
                                .unwrap_or(i64::MIN)
                        };
                        // Stable, so that ties keep the generator's order; the
                        // best gain last, since the climbs pop from the end.
                        match steer.as_ref().filter(|_| TYPE_ORDER) {
                            Some(steer) => {
                                forced.sort_by_key(|a| (gain(a), steer.prior(state, a)));
                            }
                            None => forced.sort_by_key(gain),
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        // E120: whether today's search ended before its limits.
        let ended_early = !search.spent();
        thought.forced = usize::from(exhausted);
        thought.evals = search.evals;
        thought.memory = memory.len();
        thought.plans = plans.len();

        // The plan that scores best against the whole memory and its own
        // replies, the latest on a tie. The latest is always scored; earlier ones
        // while time remains.
        let late = || limit.hard.is_some_and(|t| Instant::now() >= t);
        let mut scores: Vec<Option<i64>> = vec![None; plans.len()];
        for index in (0..plans.len()).rev() {
            if index + 1 < plans.len() && late() {
                break;
            }
            scores[index] = Some(search.final_score(&plans[index], &memory));
        }
        let pick = |scores: &[Option<i64>]| {
            let mut best: Option<(i64, usize)> = None;
            for (index, score) in scores.iter().enumerate().rev() {
                if let Some(score) = *score {
                    if best.is_none_or(|(top, _)| score > top) {
                        best = Some((score, index));
                    }
                }
            }
            best
        };
        let mut best = pick(&scores);
        // The plan played must have had its replies searched (E027): until the
        // best has, its replies are searched in the time left, the opponent's
        // climb stopping at the hard limit, and the choice made again.
        search.limit.soft = limit.hard;
        while let Some((_, index)) = best {
            if !VERIFY || plans[index].own.is_some() || late() {
                break;
            }
            let found = search.answers(&plans[index].end);
            plans[index].own = Some(found);
            thought.checks += 1;
            scores[index] = Some(search.final_score(&plans[index], &memory));
            best = pick(&scores);
        }
        if let Some(lean) = lean.filter(|lean| !lean.free || ended_early) {
            let today = best.map(|(_, index)| index);
            let chosen = search.lean_step(&plans, &scores, &memory, (today, lean), (full, opening));
            if let Some(index) = chosen {
                best = Some((scores[index].unwrap_or(i64::MIN), index));
            }
        } else if let Some(width) = deep {
            let started = Instant::now();
            for (index, score) in scores.iter_mut().enumerate() {
                score.get_or_insert_with(|| search.final_score(&plans[index], &memory));
            }
            best = pick(&scores);
            let today = best.map(|(_, index)| index);
            let deep_best = search.deepen(&plans, &scores, &memory, (today, width), limit, opening);
            if let Some(index) = deep_best {
                best = Some((scores[index].unwrap_or(i64::MIN), index));
            }
            eprintln!(
                "DEEP turn={} candidates={} leaves={} differs={} ms={:.1}",
                state.game_turn(),
                search.deep_stats.0,
                search.deep_stats.1,
                u8::from(deep_best.is_some() && deep_best != today),
                started.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1000.0
            );
        }
        thought.score = best.map(|(score, _)| score);
        if let Some((_, index)) = best {
            thought.strategic = search
                .guide
                .as_ref()
                .is_some_and(|g| !g.plan.is_empty() && plans[index].commands.starts_with(&g.plan));
            thought.pieces = search.guide.as_ref().map_or(0, |g| {
                g.pieces
                    .iter()
                    .filter(|p| p.iter().all(|c| plans[index].commands.contains(c)))
                    .count()
            });
            // Each command is checked once more, in order, on a scratch copy.
            let mut scratch = state.clone();
            for &command in &plans[index].commands {
                if scratch.apply(command) {
                    thought.commands.push(command);
                }
            }
        }
        thought
    }
}
mod session {
    //! The loop of a bot: read CodinGame's input, think, answer, flush, with the
    //! policy crate's loop (`crate::ice_and_fire_policy::io::turns`).

    use std::io::{BufRead, Write};
    use std::time::Instant;

    use crate::ice_and_fire_engine::{answer_line, League, State};
    use crate::ice_and_fire_opening::planned::Planned;
    use crate::ice_and_fire_policy::io::turns;

    use crate::search::{think, think_with, Limit};
    use crate::strategy::{self, Memory};

    /// Plays turns of a Bronze game until the input ends. `limit` gives the
    /// search's limits from the instant the turn's first line arrived and the
    /// number of the turn (1 first); `opening` plays the opening and keeps its
    /// plan between turns. Prints a debug line per turn to stderr (debug output
    /// goes there only).
    pub fn play(
        limit: &dyn Fn(Instant, u32) -> Limit,
        mut opening: Planned,
        input: impl BufRead,
        output: impl Write,
    ) -> Result<(), String> {
        // The roles of the strategic layer, kept beside the opening's plan; the
        // layer does nothing unless `strategy::STRATEGY` is set (E077).
        let mut roles = Memory::default();
        turns(
            input,
            output,
            |initial, text, turn, start| match State::read(initial, text, League::Bronze, turn) {
                Ok(state) => {
                    let layer = strategy::guide(&state, &mut roles);
                    let thought = match layer {
                        Some(guide) => {
                            think_with(&state, limit(start, turn), &mut opening, Some(guide))
                        }
                        None => think(&state, limit(start, turn), &mut opening),
                    };
                    eprintln!(
                    "turn {turn}: climbs {} tries {} memory {} checks {} forced {} strategic {} {} {:?}",
                    thought.climbs,
                    thought.evals,
                    thought.memory,
                    thought.checks,
                    thought.forced,
                    u8::from(thought.strategic),
                    thought.pieces,
                    start.elapsed()
                );
                    answer_line(&thought.commands)
                }
                Err(err) => {
                    eprintln!("plan: cannot read the input: {err}");
                    "WAIT".to_string()
                }
            },
        )
    }
}
mod strategy {
    //! The strategic layer of the frontline plan
    //! (`research/codingame/2026-11-20-frontline-plan.md`): objectives with their
    //! values, the race to them, and the roles of our units kept between turns
    //! (Steps 2 and 3), and the strategic turn offered to the search (Step 4,
    //! E077), each behind a switch.

    pub mod objectives {
        //! The objectives of a map and the land each decides.
        //!
        //! An objective is a cell of the contested band or a middle choke
        //! (`crate::eval::goal_zones`). Its value for a side is the land it gains by
        //! holding it: the number of valid cells strictly nearer (steps over valid
        //! cells) to the side's active land than to the enemy's, with the cell added
        //! to its land, less the same count as it is (the enemy's land unchanged).
        //! For a cell the side already holds, the land it would lose: the count as
        //! it is less the count with the cell removed. With [`VALUE_SWING`] the value
        //! is instead the swing of the review tool's `codingame-roles`: the count
        //! with the cell added to the side's land less the count with it added to
        //! the enemy's.

        use crate::ice_and_fire_engine::{Bits, State, CELLS, HQ};
        use crate::ice_and_fire_opening::econ::distances;

        use crate::eval::goal_zones;

        /// The least value for an objective to count: `None` counts every objective
        /// that gains land (value above 0), `Some(3)` is the first cut.
        pub const OBJECTIVE_MIN_VALUE: Option<i64> = None;

        /// Whether the value is the swing (the land with the cell held by us less
        /// held by the enemy) rather than the land gained.
        pub const VALUE_SWING: bool = false;

        /// What kind of cell an objective is.
        #[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
        pub enum Kind {
            /// A middle choke (also when it is in the band).
            Choke,
            /// A cell of the contested band.
            Band,
        }

        /// An objective for one side.
        #[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
        pub struct Objective {
            pub cell: usize,
            pub kind: Kind,
            /// Whether the side holds it: it is one of its active cells.
            pub held: bool,
            /// The land it decides.
            pub value: i64,
        }

        /// The objectives of `state` for `seat`, by value, highest first, then
        /// chokes before band cells, then by cell.
        pub fn objectives(state: &State, seat: usize) -> Vec<Objective> {
            objectives_valued(state, seat, VALUE_SWING)
        }

        /// [`objectives`] with the value as the swing (`swing`) or as the land
        /// gained.
        pub fn objectives_valued(state: &State, seat: usize, swing: bool) -> Vec<Objective> {
            let (band, chokes) = goal_zones(state);
            let (mine, theirs) = (state.active(seat), state.active(1 - seat));
            let (dm, dt) = (distances(state, mine), distances(state, theirs));
            let base = nearer(state, &dm, &dm, &dt);
            let mut out = Vec::new();
            for cell in (band | chokes).iter() {
                let dg = distances(state, Bits::cell(cell));
                let held = mine.test(cell);
                let value = if swing {
                    nearer(state, &dm, &dg, &dt) - nearer(state, &dt, &dg, &dm)
                } else if held {
                    let without = distances(state, flood_without(mine, seat, cell));
                    base - nearer(state, &without, &without, &dt)
                } else {
                    nearer(state, &dm, &dg, &dt) - base
                };
                out.push(Objective {
                    cell,
                    kind: if chokes.test(cell) {
                        Kind::Choke
                    } else {
                        Kind::Band
                    },
                    held,
                    value,
                });
            }
            out.sort_by_key(|o| (-o.value, o.kind != Kind::Choke, o.cell));
            out
        }

        /// The valid cells strictly nearer to the land of distances `a` plus the
        /// cell of distances `g` than to the land of distances `b`.
        fn nearer(state: &State, a: &[u8; CELLS], g: &[u8; CELLS], b: &[u8; CELLS]) -> i64 {
            let mut n = 0;
            for c in state.map().valid.iter() {
                let d = a[c].min(g[c]);
                if d != u8::MAX && d < b[c] {
                    n += 1;
                }
            }
            n
        }

        /// The objectives that count: of value at least [`OBJECTIVE_MIN_VALUE`], or
        /// above 0 when there is none.
        pub fn counted(objectives: &[Objective]) -> Vec<Objective> {
            objectives
                .iter()
                .filter(|o| o.value >= OBJECTIVE_MIN_VALUE.unwrap_or(1))
                .copied()
                .collect()
        }

        /// The active land of `seat` if `cell` were not its: what is still joined
        /// to its HQ over the rest of `active`.
        fn flood_without(active: Bits, seat: usize, cell: usize) -> Bits {
            let rest = active.and_not(Bits::cell(cell));
            let mut reached = Bits::cell(HQ[seat]) & rest;
            loop {
                let next = reached | (reached.neighbours() & rest);
                if next == reached {
                    return reached;
                }
                reached = next;
            }
        }
    }
    pub mod race {
        //! The race to each objective we do not hold: when each side can first be
        //! there, in turns of the side.
        //!
        //! A unit arrives in its map distance. A training arrives in 1 (the unit
        //! cannot move the turn it is trained) plus the map distance from the side's
        //! nearest trainable cell (a valid cell next to its active land that a
        //! level-1 unit may enter), plus the turns of income the side needs to
        //! afford the unit (10 gold) if it cannot now; with no income it never can.
        //! The side's arrival is the smaller, a unit winning a tie. We act first in
        //! a turn, so a tie is ours.

        use crate::ice_and_fire_engine::State;

        use super::objectives::Objective;

        /// The gold of a level-1 unit.
        const TRAIN_COST: i64 = 10;
        /// The arrival turn counted for a side that cannot arrive, in `margin`.
        const NEVER: i64 = 100;

        /// How a side arrives.
        #[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
        pub enum How {
            /// By the unit of this id.
            Unit(u32),
            /// By a training on this cell.
            Train(usize),
        }

        /// A side's arrival at an objective.
        #[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
        pub struct Arrival {
            pub turns: u32,
            pub how: How,
        }

        /// The race to one objective.
        #[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
        pub struct Race {
            pub cell: usize,
            /// Our best arrival.
            pub ours: Option<Arrival>,
            /// Our arrival by a training, whether or not it is the best.
            pub ours_training: Option<Arrival>,
            /// The enemy's best arrival.
            pub theirs: Option<Arrival>,
            /// The enemy's arrival turn less ours (a side that cannot arrive counts
            /// as 100): 0 or more means we are there first or tied.
            pub margin: i64,
        }

        /// The races of the objectives `seat` does not hold.
        pub fn race(state: &State, seat: usize, objectives: &[Objective]) -> Vec<Race> {
            let mut out = Vec::new();
            for objective in objectives.iter().filter(|o| !o.held) {
                let cell = objective.cell;
                let (ours_unit, ours_training) = arrivals(state, seat, cell);
                let ours = best(ours_unit, ours_training);
                let (their_unit, their_training) = arrivals(state, 1 - seat, cell);
                let theirs = best(their_unit, their_training);
                let turns = |a: Option<Arrival>| a.map_or(NEVER, |a| i64::from(a.turns));
                out.push(Race {
                    cell,
                    ours,
                    ours_training,
                    theirs,
                    margin: turns(theirs) - turns(ours),
                });
            }
            out
        }

        /// The smaller arrival, the unit's on a tie.
        fn best(unit: Option<Arrival>, training: Option<Arrival>) -> Option<Arrival> {
            match (unit, training) {
                (Some(u), Some(t)) => Some(if t.turns < u.turns { t } else { u }),
                (u, t) => u.or(t),
            }
        }

        /// The arrival of `side` at `cell` by a unit and by a training.
        fn arrivals(state: &State, side: usize, cell: usize) -> (Option<Arrival>, Option<Arrival>) {
            let map = state.map();
            let mut unit: Option<Arrival> = None;
            for from in state.units(side).iter() {
                let d = map.distance(from, cell);
                let Some(id) = state.unit_id(from) else {
                    continue;
                };
                if d != u8::MAX && unit.is_none_or(|u| u32::from(d) < u.turns) {
                    unit = Some(Arrival {
                        turns: u32::from(d),
                        how: How::Unit(id),
                    });
                }
            }
            // A player's income is paid at the start of its own turn (RULES.md,
            // "Start of a player's turn"): ours is in the gold already, the other
            // side's is still to come.
            let gold = state.gold(side)
                + if side == state.to_act() {
                    0
                } else {
                    state.income(side)
                };
            let wait = match (gold, state.income(side)) {
                (gold, _) if gold >= TRAIN_COST => Some(0),
                (_, income) if income <= 0 => None,
                (gold, income) => Some((TRAIN_COST - gold + income - 1) / income),
            };
            let mut training: Option<Arrival> = None;
            if let Some(wait) = wait {
                let trainable =
                    state.active(side).neighbours() & map.valid & state.enterable(side, 1);
                for from in trainable.iter() {
                    let d = map.distance(from, cell);
                    if d != u8::MAX
                        && training.is_none_or(|t| 1 + wait as u32 + u32::from(d) < t.turns)
                    {
                        training = Some(Arrival {
                            turns: 1 + wait as u32 + u32::from(d),
                            how: How::Train(from),
                        });
                    }
                }
            }
            (unit, training)
        }
    }
    pub mod roles {
        //! The roles of our units: at most one frontline unit per counted objective
        //! we can reach first or at the same time, kept between turns.
        //!
        //! Rules of [`assign`]:
        //! - Only counted objectives (`objectives::counted`: every one that gains
        //!   land, or those of value at least `OBJECTIVE_MIN_VALUE`) that we do not
        //!   hold and whose race margin is 0 or more take a role, in rank order
        //!   (value, chokes first, then our arrival, then cell), while the side can
        //!   cover them: a free unit, or a training it can pay for.
        //! - A unit keeps its objective while it lives and the objective takes a
        //!   role, unless another unit that is not frontline is nearer to it by at
        //!   least one step: the handover, the old unit going to the back line (and
        //!   staying there for this turn).
        //! - The other such objectives, by value then our arrival, take the
        //!   nearest free unit, or a training when that is as near or nearer
        //!   (`Race::ours_training` before the unit): the cell to train on is then
        //!   listed instead of a unit. A training cell serves one objective (the best
        //!   ranked), and trainings are assigned only while the gold left after
        //!   those already assigned pays 10 for one.

        use std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};

        use crate::ice_and_fire_engine::{Bits, State};

        use super::objectives::{counted, Kind, Objective};
        use super::race::{How, Race};

        /// The gold of a level-1 unit.
        const TRAIN_COST: i64 = 10;

        /// The objective cell of each frontline unit, by unit id, between turns.
        #[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]
        pub struct Memory {
            pub objective_of: BTreeMap<u32, usize>,
        }

        /// The roles of one turn.
        #[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]
        pub struct Roles {
            /// Frontline units, with their objective cells, by objective order.
            pub frontline: Vec<(u32, usize)>,
            /// The cell to train on, with the objective it serves.
            pub trainings: Vec<(usize, usize)>,
            /// The other units, by id.
            pub back: Vec<u32>,
        }

        /// The roles of the units of `seat`, `memory` read and updated.
        pub fn assign(
            state: &State,
            seat: usize,
            objectives: &[Objective],
            races: &[Race],
            memory: &mut Memory,
        ) -> Roles {
            assign_among(state, seat, objectives, races, memory, state.units(seat))
        }

        /// [`assign`] with only the units on `eligible` cells taking a frontline
        /// role (E077's back units walking); the others are back-line units.
        pub fn assign_among(
            state: &State,
            seat: usize,
            objectives: &[Objective],
            races: &[Race],
            memory: &mut Memory,
            eligible: Bits,
        ) -> Roles {
            let map = state.map();
            // The units of ours that may take a role, by id, with their cells.
            let units: BTreeMap<u32, usize> = (state.units(seat) & eligible)
                .iter()
                .filter_map(|c| state.unit_id(c).map(|id| (id, c)))
                .collect();
            // The objectives that take a role, in order: value, our arrival, cell.
            let mut open: Vec<(Objective, Race)> = Vec::new();
            for o in counted(objectives).into_iter().filter(|o| !o.held) {
                if let Some(r) = races.iter().find(|r| r.cell == o.cell) {
                    if r.ours.is_some() && r.margin >= 0 {
                        open.push((o, *r));
                    }
                }
            }
            open.sort_by_key(|(o, r)| {
                (
                    -o.value,
                    o.kind != Kind::Choke,
                    r.ours.map_or(u32::MAX, |a| a.turns),
                    o.cell,
                )
            });

            let dist = |unit: u32, goal: usize| u32::from(map.distance(units[&unit], goal));
            let in_play = |holder: &BTreeMap<usize, u32>, released: &BTreeSet<u32>, id: u32| {
                released.contains(&id) || holder.values().any(|&u| u == id)
            };

            // Keep the roles of the units that live and whose objectives still take
            // one (the lowest id on an objective two units hold).
            let mut holder: BTreeMap<usize, u32> = BTreeMap::new(); // objective -> unit
            for (&id, &goal) in &memory.objective_of {
                if units.contains_key(&id)
                    && open.iter().any(|(o, _)| o.cell == goal)
                    && !holder.contains_key(&goal)
                {
                    holder.insert(goal, id);
                }
            }

            // The handover: a unit that is not frontline and is nearer by a step.
            let mut released: BTreeSet<u32> = BTreeSet::new();
            for (o, _) in &open {
                let Some(&keeper) = holder.get(&o.cell) else {
                    continue;
                };
                let nearest = units
                    .keys()
                    .copied()
                    .filter(|&id| !in_play(&holder, &released, id))
                    .map(|id| (dist(id, o.cell), id))
                    .filter(|&(d, _)| d != u32::from(u8::MAX))
                    .min();
                if let Some((d, id)) = nearest {
                    if d < dist(keeper, o.cell) {
                        released.insert(keeper);
                        holder.insert(o.cell, id);
                    }
                }
            }

            // The objectives left: the nearest free unit, or a training.
            let mut trainings = Vec::new();
            for (o, r) in &open {
                if holder.contains_key(&o.cell) {
                    continue;
                }
                let free = units
                    .keys()
                    .copied()
                    .filter(|&id| !in_play(&holder, &released, id))
                    .map(|id| (dist(id, o.cell), id))
                    .filter(|&(d, _)| d != u32::from(u8::MAX))
                    .min();
                let unit_turns = free.map(|(d, _)| i64::from(d));
                // A training needs a cell no better objective uses and the gold
                // left after the trainings already assigned.
                let train = r.ours_training.and_then(|t| match t.how {
                    How::Train(cell)
                        if state.gold(seat) - TRAIN_COST * trainings.len() as i64 >= TRAIN_COST
                            && !trainings.iter().any(|&(c, _)| c == cell) =>
                    {
                        Some((cell, i64::from(t.turns)))
                    }
                    _ => None,
                });
                let train_turns = train.map(|(_, t)| t);
                let use_train = match (unit_turns, train_turns) {
                    (Some(u), Some(t)) => t < u,
                    (None, Some(_)) => true,
                    _ => false,
                };
                let chosen = if use_train { train_turns } else { unit_turns };
                let Some(turns) = chosen else {
                    continue;
                };
                if r.theirs.map_or(100, |a| i64::from(a.turns)) < turns {
                    continue;
                }
                match (use_train, train, free) {
                    (true, Some((cell, _)), _) => trainings.push((cell, o.cell)),
                    (false, _, Some((_, id))) => {
                        holder.insert(o.cell, id);
                    }
                    _ => {}
                }
            }

            let mut out = Roles {
                trainings,
                ..Roles::default()
            };
            for (o, _) in &open {
                if let Some(&id) = holder.get(&o.cell) {
                    out.frontline.push((id, o.cell));
                }
            }
            out.back = state
                .units(seat)
                .iter()
                .filter_map(|c| state.unit_id(c))
                .filter(|id| !out.frontline.iter().any(|&(u, _)| u == *id))
                .collect();
            out.back.sort_unstable();
            memory.objective_of = out.frontline.iter().copied().collect();
            out
        }
    }
    pub mod turn {
        //! The strategic turn (Step 4 of the frontline plan, E077): one plan made of
        //! the frontline units' steps toward their objectives, then trainings at
        //! their tips within the gold, then (with [`super::TRAININGS`] at 2) the
        //! trainings the roles give the objectives no unit covers. The back-line
        //! units are left to the search, which goes on climbing from the plan.
        //!
        //! Every command is checked on a scratch copy, in order, so the plan applies
        //! whole on the state it was made for.

        use crate::ice_and_fire_engine::{Bits, Command, State};

        use super::roles::Roles;
        use crate::actions::xy;
        use crate::eval::threatened;

        /// The gold of a level-1 unit.
        const TRAIN_COST: i64 = 10;

        /// The cell of the unit `id` of `seat`, if it lives.
        fn cell_of(state: &State, seat: usize, id: u32) -> Option<usize> {
            state
                .units(seat)
                .iter()
                .find(|&c| state.unit_id(c) == Some(id))
        }

        /// The cells next to `from` one step nearer to `goal`, the cells not ours
        /// first (a step that takes land), then by cell.
        fn steps_toward(state: &State, seat: usize, from: usize, goal: usize) -> Vec<usize> {
            let map = state.map();
            let here = map.distance(from, goal);
            if here == u8::MAX || here == 0 {
                return Vec::new();
            }
            let mut out: Vec<usize> = (Bits::cell(from).neighbours() & map.valid)
                .iter()
                .filter(|&n| map.distance(n, goal) < here)
                .collect();
            out.sort_by_key(|&n| (state.owned(seat).test(n), n));
            out
        }

        /// Applies `command` on `scratch` and adds it to `out` if the rules accept
        /// it; whether they did.
        fn accepted(scratch: &mut State, out: &mut Vec<Command>, command: Command) -> bool {
            let ok = scratch.apply(command);
            if ok {
                out.push(command);
            }
            ok
        }

        /// How the strategic turn keeps the line behind its frontline units (E077,
        /// round 2, after the diagnosis that a third of its steps left a cell the
        /// enemy then entered).
        #[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]
        pub struct Rules {
            /// Also the trainings the roles give the objectives no unit covers.
            pub role_trainings: bool,
            /// A step off a cell the enemy can reach next turn needs that cell
            /// guarded at once: 0, no (round 1); 1, by a tower; 2, by a level-1
            /// training. A step whose guard the rules or the gold refuse is not
            /// played.
            pub guard: u8,
            /// The tip training of a unit that left a cell the enemy can reach goes
            /// on that cell instead, when it is still empty.
            pub fill_behind: bool,
            /// A step is not played when it raises the cells of ours the enemy can
            /// take at its next turn (`eval::threatened`).
            pub safe_step: bool,
        }

        /// The pieces of the strategic turn (E077, [`super::TURN`]'s 4): for each
        /// frontline unit, its step toward its objective and the training at its
        /// tip that the gold pays, each made alone from `state`, the units in role
        /// order; pieces the rules refuse are left out.
        pub fn pieces(state: &State, roles: &Roles, rules: Rules) -> Vec<Vec<Command>> {
            let mut out = Vec::new();
            for &(id, goal) in &roles.frontline {
                let one = Roles {
                    frontline: vec![(id, goal)],
                    ..Roles::default()
                };
                let piece = strategic_turn(
                    state,
                    &one,
                    Rules {
                        role_trainings: false,
                        ..rules
                    },
                );
                if !piece.is_empty() {
                    out.push(piece);
                }
            }
            out
        }

        /// The step of the unit `id` from `from` to `to` on `scratch`, with the
        /// guard `rules` ask for on `from` when the enemy reaches it (`exposed`):
        /// the commands, or `None` when the step is not played.
        fn step(
            scratch: &State,
            id: u32,
            from: usize,
            to: usize,
            exposed: bool,
            rules: Rules,
        ) -> Option<Vec<Command>> {
            let seat = scratch.to_act();
            let mut trial = scratch.clone();
            let mut commands = Vec::new();
            let (x, y) = xy(to);
            if !accepted(&mut trial, &mut commands, Command::Move { id, x, y }) {
                return None;
            }
            if exposed && rules.guard != 0 {
                let (fx, fy) = xy(from);
                let guard = if rules.guard == 1 {
                    Command::BuildTower { x: fx, y: fy }
                } else {
                    Command::Train {
                        level: 1,
                        x: fx,
                        y: fy,
                    }
                };
                if !accepted(&mut trial, &mut commands, guard) {
                    return None;
                }
            }
            if rules.safe_step && threatened(&trial, seat) > threatened(scratch, seat) {
                return None;
            }
            Some(commands)
        }

        /// The commands of the strategic turn of the player to act in `state`, with
        /// `roles` its roles this turn, by `rules`.
        pub fn strategic_turn(state: &State, roles: &Roles, rules: Rules) -> Vec<Command> {
            let seat = state.to_act();
            let map = state.map();
            let mut scratch = state.clone();
            let mut out = Vec::new();
            // The cells the enemy can take at its next turn, as the turn starts.
            let reach = crate::eval::reach(state, 1 - seat);
            // The exposed cells our frontline units left unguarded, by unit.
            let mut left: Vec<(u32, usize)> = Vec::new();

            // 1. The frontline units step toward their objectives.
            for &(id, goal) in &roles.frontline {
                let Some(from) = cell_of(&scratch, seat, id) else {
                    continue;
                };
                if !scratch.movable_units().test(from) {
                    continue;
                }
                let exposed = reach.test(from);
                for to in steps_toward(&scratch, seat, from, goal) {
                    if let Some(commands) = step(&scratch, id, from, to, exposed, rules) {
                        for command in &commands {
                            scratch.apply(*command);
                        }
                        if exposed && rules.guard == 0 {
                            left.push((id, from));
                        }
                        out.extend(commands);
                        break;
                    }
                }
            }

            // 2. A training at the tip of each frontline unit: on a cell next to it
            // nearer its objective, the nearest first; with `fill_behind`, on the
            // exposed cell it left instead.
            for &(id, goal) in &roles.frontline {
                if scratch.gold(seat) < TRAIN_COST {
                    break;
                }
                let Some(at) = cell_of(&scratch, seat, id) else {
                    continue;
                };
                let behind = left.iter().find(|&&(u, _)| u == id).map(|&(_, c)| c);
                let cells = match behind {
                    Some(cell) if rules.fill_behind => vec![cell],
                    _ => steps_toward(&scratch, seat, at, goal),
                };
                for to in cells {
                    let (x, y) = xy(to);
                    if accepted(&mut scratch, &mut out, Command::Train { level: 1, x, y }) {
                        break;
                    }
                }
            }

            // 3. The objectives no unit covers: a training at our trainable cell
            // nearest each, after the moves.
            if rules.role_trainings {
                for &(_, goal) in &roles.trainings {
                    if scratch.gold(seat) < TRAIN_COST {
                        break;
                    }
                    let trainable = scratch.active(seat).neighbours() & map.valid;
                    let mut cells: Vec<usize> = trainable
                        .iter()
                        .filter(|&c| map.distance(c, goal) != u8::MAX)
                        .collect();
                    cells.sort_by_key(|&c| (map.distance(c, goal), c));
                    for to in cells {
                        let (x, y) = xy(to);
                        if accepted(&mut scratch, &mut out, Command::Train { level: 1, x, y }) {
                            break;
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            out
        }
    }

    use crate::ice_and_fire_engine::{Command, State};

    pub use roles::Memory;

    /// How the strategic turn reaches the search (E077), bits added: 0, not at
    /// all (v031); 1, offered as one macro action at the climbs' root; 2, the
    /// first climb of each turn starts with it; 4, its pieces (each frontline
    /// unit's step and the training at its tip) offered as macro actions at
    /// every step of the climbs.
    pub const TURN: u8 = 0;

    /// Which trainings the strategic turn holds (E077): 1, at the frontline
    /// units' tips only, after their moves (the owner's rule); 2, also the
    /// trainings the roles give the objectives no unit covers, after those.
    pub const TRAININGS: u8 = 1;

    /// The objectives' term in the search's score (E077), in quarters of a cell
    /// of land per cell an objective decides; 0 for none (v031).
    pub const OBJECTIVE_QUARTERS: i64 = 0;

    /// What the objectives' term counts for an objective of value `v`: with
    /// false, `v` if we hold it, `-v` if the enemy does, 0 otherwise; with true,
    /// a neutral objective counts `v` times our race margin at the turn's start
    /// clamped to -1..=1 (the plan's definition).
    pub const OBJECTIVE_RACE: bool = false;

    /// How the strategic turn keeps the line behind its frontline units (E077,
    /// round 2): see [`turn::Rules`]. [`GUARD`]: 0 none (round 1), 1 a tower, 2
    /// a level-1 training on the exposed cell a unit leaves.
    pub const GUARD: u8 = 0;
    /// See [`GUARD`]: the tip training fills the exposed cell left.
    pub const FILL_BEHIND: bool = false;
    /// See [`GUARD`]: no step that raises our cells the enemy can take.
    pub const SAFE_STEP: bool = false;
    /// Whether only units on cells the enemy cannot reach next turn take a
    /// frontline role (E077, round 2): the units holding the border keep it.
    pub const BACK_ONLY: bool = false;

    /// The first and the last game turn of the strategic layer (E077: 7 to 14).
    pub const FROM_TURN: u32 = 7;
    /// See [`FROM_TURN`].
    pub const UNTIL_TURN: u32 = 14;

    /// Whether the bot computes objectives, races and roles each turn: when the
    /// strategic turn or the objectives' term is on.
    pub const STRATEGY: bool = TURN != 0 || OBJECTIVE_QUARTERS != 0;

    /// What the layer gives the search for one turn.
    #[derive(Clone, Debug, Default)]
    pub struct Guide {
        /// The strategic turn's commands, empty for none.
        pub plan: Vec<Command>,
        /// Whether the plan is offered as a macro action.
        pub offered: bool,
        /// Whether the first climb starts with the plan.
        pub start: bool,
        /// The plan's pieces offered as macro actions, empty for none.
        pub pieces: Vec<Vec<Command>>,
        /// For the objectives' term: each objective's cell, value and the count
        /// it gets when neither side holds it (`OBJECTIVE_RACE`).
        pub objectives: Vec<(usize, i64, i64)>,
        /// The term's weight in quarters.
        pub quarters: i64,
    }

    impl Guide {
        /// The objectives' term for `seat` in `state`.
        pub fn term(&self, state: &State, seat: usize) -> i64 {
            if self.quarters == 0 {
                return 0;
            }
            let (mine, theirs) = (state.active(seat), state.active(1 - seat));
            let mut total = 0;
            for &(cell, value, neutral) in &self.objectives {
                total += if mine.test(cell) {
                    value
                } else if theirs.test(cell) {
                    -value
                } else {
                    neutral
                };
            }
            self.quarters * total / 4
        }
    }

    /// The layer's guide for the turn of `state`, `memory` updated; none
    /// outside game turns [`FROM_TURN`] to [`UNTIL_TURN`] or when [`STRATEGY`]
    /// is off.
    pub fn guide(state: &State, memory: &mut Memory) -> Option<Guide> {
        let now = state.game_turn();
        if !STRATEGY || !(FROM_TURN..=UNTIL_TURN).contains(&now) || state.outcome().is_some() {
            return None;
        }
        guide_with(state, memory, SETTINGS)
    }

    /// The switches of the layer, together.
    #[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]
    pub struct Settings {
        /// [`TURN`].
        pub mode: u8,
        /// The strategic turn's rules ([`TRAININGS`], [`GUARD`],
        /// [`FILL_BEHIND`], [`SAFE_STEP`]).
        pub rules: turn::Rules,
        /// [`BACK_ONLY`].
        pub back_only: bool,
        /// [`OBJECTIVE_QUARTERS`].
        pub quarters: i64,
        /// [`OBJECTIVE_RACE`].
        pub race_counts: bool,
    }

    /// The bot's switches.
    pub const SETTINGS: Settings = Settings {
        mode: TURN,
        rules: turn::Rules {
            role_trainings: TRAININGS == 2,
            guard: GUARD,
            fill_behind: FILL_BEHIND,
            safe_step: SAFE_STEP,
        },
        back_only: BACK_ONLY,
        quarters: OBJECTIVE_QUARTERS,
        race_counts: OBJECTIVE_RACE,
    };

    /// [`guide`] with its switches given, at any game turn.
    pub fn guide_with(state: &State, memory: &mut Memory, settings: Settings) -> Option<Guide> {
        let Settings {
            mode,
            rules,
            back_only,
            quarters,
            race_counts,
        } = settings;
        let seat = state.to_act();
        let objectives = objectives::objectives(state, seat);
        let races = race::race(state, seat, &objectives);
        let roles = if back_only {
            let eligible = state
                .units(seat)
                .and_not(crate::eval::reach(state, 1 - seat));
            roles::assign_among(state, seat, &objectives, &races, memory, eligible)
        } else {
            roles::assign(state, seat, &objectives, &races, memory)
        };
        let plan = if mode != 0 {
            turn::strategic_turn(state, &roles, rules)
        } else {
            Vec::new()
        };
        let counted = objectives::counted(&objectives);
        let terms = counted
            .iter()
            .map(|o| {
                let margin = races
                    .iter()
                    .find(|r| r.cell == o.cell)
                    .map_or(0, |r| r.margin.clamp(-1, 1));
                let neutral = if race_counts { o.value * margin } else { 0 };
                (o.cell, o.value, neutral)
            })
            .collect();
        let parts = if mode & 4 != 0 {
            turn::pieces(state, &roles, rules)
        } else {
            Vec::new()
        };
        Some(Guide {
            pieces: parts,
            offered: !plan.is_empty() && mode & 1 != 0,
            start: !plan.is_empty() && mode & 2 != 0,
            plan,
            objectives: terms,
            quarters,
        })
    }
}
